&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s the bit about us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fireblocks is an enterprise-grade platform delivering a secure infrastructure for moving, storing, and issuing digital assets &amp;amp; cryptocurrencies. At Fireblocks, we enable businesses to securely build, run and scale digital asset operations through the Fireblocks Network and MPC-based Wallet Infrastructure. Our next-generation multi-layer technology protects Digital assets from cyber-attacks, internal collusion, and human error. Fireblocks is the only platform that provides insurance for digital assets in storage, transfer, and E&amp;amp;O.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As of January 2026, we serve over 2,400 institutional customers, have secured the transfer of over $14 trillion in digital assets, and are the world’s highest-valued digital asset infrastructure company, with over $1 billion raised.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is simple: Enable every business to easily and securely support digital assets &amp;amp; cryptocurrencies. Come join us as we&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Secure. Simplify. Scale&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s the bit about the opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Fireblocks sales team, you will play a meaningful role in scaling one of the fastest-growing companies in the Blockchain and Cybersecurity field. You’ll target a mixture of Crypto-Native and Financial Services accounts in the DACH (Germany, Austria &amp;amp; Switzerland) region, working closely with Sales Engineers and the Business Development team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieving monthly and quarterly revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the Fireblocks BDR and GTM Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and maintaining relationships with prospects and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect, territory, and account planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Updating and maintaining Fireblocks CRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise sales experience in software or institutional sales, selling into a relevant space of financial services, crypto, blockchain or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of blockchain technology and cryptocurrency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working within financial services, cybersecurity, or cryptocurrency is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of over-achievement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial and relentless hunting attitude with a willingness to prospect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked in a team-selling environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a comprehensive onboarding and training program for all new employees. We are looking for those who want to work with some of the industry’s most talented contributors. You should bring a track record of success and experience closing complex deals within the financial services or fintech sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For employees hired to work from the EU, Fireblocks is required by law to include a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. This range is specific to&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Germany and takes into consideration a wide range of factors that are reviewed when making a hiring decision, such as years of experience, skills, and other business needs. It is not typical for a candidate to be hired at or near the top of the pay range and each compensation decision is dependent on each individual case. A reasonable base salary range estimate for this position is&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;€80,400 – €110,550.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary is one component of the total compensation package, which for some roles may include a target bonus, a very competitive equity grant, and very generous benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;While we believe competitive compensation is a critical aspect of your decision to join us, we do hope you also spend time considering why our mission and culture are right for you. We are creating something transformational here, and we hope you are as excited about the future as we are.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Please see our candidate privacy policy here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/fireblocks/sales-director-dach-berlin-berlin-342040","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin, Berlin","created_at":1794034514},{"slug":"remote-senior-design-engineer-deel-395604","company_name":"Hirehire","title":"Senior Design Engineer | Deel","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role:</strong> Senior Design Engineer</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Company:</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.deel.com">Deel</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> United Kingdom, Israel, Portugal, Spain, Czech Republic, Poland, France, Switzerland, Hungary, Ireland, Sweden, Germany or Estonia</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Job Type:</strong> Full-time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About Deel</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deel is the all-in-one payroll and HR platform for global teams. HRIS, payroll, compliance, benefits, performance and equipment management sit in one product. It supports every worker type in 150+ countries. In 2024, Deel paid $11.2 billion to workers in nearly 100 currencies and provided healthcare and benefits in 109 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The company has a $17.3 billion valuation and reached $1 billion in ARR in just over five years. About 7,000 people work at Deel, across more than 100 countries and 74 languages. Customers rate it 4.83 on average, from 15,000 reviews on G2, Trustpilot, Capterra, Apple and Google.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most teams use AI as a faster way for humans to build products. Deel wants to go further and build the system that lets AI build the products. Humans set the taste, the guardrails and the standards it works within.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That system is your product. You build what AI generates against: the design system and component architecture, the generation and agent workflows, the quality gates that keep output production-ready, and the feedback loops that keep it all visible to the team. You stay hands-on as a designer, because the quickest way to prove the system works is to ship real interfaces on top of it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior individual contributor role in Product Design. You split your time between Figma and a code editor in roughly equal measure. You work directly with design leadership to drive AI adoption across the whole design organisation, and you sit in a cross-functional team with Engineering and Product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you are expected to do:</h2><h3>Build the system</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architect the design system, tokens and components as the substrate AI generates against.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design prompt libraries, patterns and agent workflows that turn design intent into production-ready UI with minimal human assembly.</p></li></ul><h3>Prove it by designing</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay a practising designer. Explore concepts quickly and design real interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prototype in production front-end code. You are the first and toughest test of whether the system produces excellent, shippable work.</p></li></ul><h3>Own quality, guardrails and evals</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define production-readiness criteria for AI-generated UI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set design-to-code fidelity benchmarks, regression safeguards and evaluation methods that keep AI output honest. Speed must not cost craft.</p></li></ul><h3>Drive the AI workflow across the design org</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with design leadership to maintain, evolve and roll out the AI-native workflow across the whole design organisation, not only your own work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Treat it as an ongoing responsibility. Drive adoption, keep standards current as tools change, and embed the workflow across teams so it never depends on one person.</p></li></ul><h3>Work across functions</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with Engineering, Product and design-system contributors. You complement engineering and do not replace it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the system round-tripping to shared surfaces such as Figma. AI-accelerated output stays visible and open to feedback, never a black box.</p></li></ul><h3>Push into generative UI</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take AI beyond the build process and into the product itself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prototype and evaluate adaptive, AI-generated interfaces as a product capability, and help decide where they belong on the roadmap.</p></li></ul><h3>Level up the team</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn what works into playbooks, prompt libraries and enablement. The wider design org builds on the system and does not depend on you. The goal is durable capability, not tool dependency.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What you need to succeed:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You move fluidly between design and code. You don't need to be the deepest specialist in either. You can design something well, build it yourself, and use AI to move quickly between the two.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have real taste for layout, typography, interaction and motion, and you care about polish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable writing TypeScript and React, including HTML, CSS and animation. You prototype fast and get from idea to working interface in hours rather than days, moving between Figma and code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have built or extended design systems that others rely on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You already use AI design and coding tools in real work, and you want to help shape new ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 7+ years in product design and front-end engineering on complex products. You are comfortable with ambiguity, and you set standards others follow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What you get:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stock grant opportunities, depending on your role, employment status and location.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional perks and benefits based on your employment status and country.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optional flexible working office membership with IWG.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/hirehire/remote-senior-design-engineer-deel-395604","tags":["Product Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1794033628},{"slug":"key-account-executive-germany-80712","company_name":"Sine Engineering","title":"Key Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Sine Engineering</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sine Engineering builds the technology behind reliable drone autonomy, delivering communication, navigation, and control systems that enable coordinated multi-drone operations. More than 200 UAV manufacturers rely on our solutions, and our technology powers many of the interceptor operations active today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Through our dual-use platform, we support civilian innovation while helping democratic nations strengthen their technological advantage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Any drone. Any scale. Anywhere.</strong> Resilient communication, navigation, and coordination built for the age of autonomy. Our products have already proven their effectiveness in real combat conditions in Ukraine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and expand Sine Engineering's customer and partner network across Germany.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify, engage, and develop strategic accounts across the defense, aerospace, UAV manufacturing, systems integration, robotics, electronics, telecommunications, RF, autonomy, and other related technology sectors.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full sales cycle, including market mapping, prospecting, qualification, discovery, technical evaluation, proposal development, negotiation, closing, and long-term account growth.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop relationships with OEMs, system integrators, defense primes, technology partners, and relevant government-affiliated stakeholders.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build direct relationships with senior executives and C-level decision-makers while developing strong engagement across engineering, program management, and procurement functions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Position Sine Engineering effectively before formal procurement and tender processes begin.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead customer discussions related to communication modules, GNSS-denied navigation systems, video links, embedded autonomy software, and integration opportunities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate technical evaluations, pilot projects, demonstrations, and integration discussions in collaboration with product and engineering teams.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare commercial proposals, pricing structures, contract documentation, and partnership models.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead commercial negotiations, including pricing, volume commitments, long-term agreements, and commercial frameworks.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain high standards of CRM management, pipeline tracking, revenue forecasting, and account planning in line with European business operations.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide market intelligence regarding German defense procurement, competitors, customer requirements, funding priorities, and partnership opportunities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Sine Engineering at industry events, trade shows, conferences, and customer meetings across Germany and Europe.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help establish scalable and repeatable sales processes for the German market and contribute to future team growth.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the Managing Director Germany to ensure commercial account ownership and local market representation remain aligned and complementary.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in B2B sales, business development, strategic account management, or partnerships within a complex technical environment. Experience in the defense, aerospace, UAV, robotics, telecommunications, RF, or deep-tech sectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of managing full-cycle sales processes with enterprise, industrial, defense, aerospace, or technology customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of long sales cycles, multi-stakeholder procurement processes, and complex commercial negotiations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to understand technical products and translate customer needs into clear business and technical requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience collaborating closely with engineering, product, operations, legal, and executive leadership teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent commercial judgment, negotiation skills, and executive-level communication abilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work independently, proactively creating opportunities rather than relying primarily on inbound leads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong sense of ownership and ability to thrive in a fast-paced, scale-up environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work effectively in a matrix organization, collaborating with both a functional sales manager and a local managing director.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Munich or willing to travel there regularly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel frequently across Germany, Ukraine, and Europe.<br /><br /><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building a market presence, territory, or sales function from an early stage.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with international teams, particularly across Germany and Eastern Europe.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience negotiating framework agreements and other long-term commercial partnerships.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about building technology that shapes the future of drone autonomy and want your work to have a meaningful impact on defense and security, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this role aligns with your experience and ambitions, don't hesitate to apply. We're looking for people who share our drive to push the boundaries of what's possible and deliver technologies that make a real-world difference.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/sine-engineering/key-account-executive-germany-80712","tags":["Business Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1794033628},{"slug":"it-cloud-manager-krumbach-269315","company_name":"Everfield","title":"IT & Cloud Manager (m/w/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>IT &amp; Cloud Manager (m/w/d)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Krumbach-Niederraunau, Bayern · Hybrid · Vollzeit, unbefristet</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Über Everfield</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everfield übernimmt, entwickelt und skaliert europäische Softwareunternehmen aus vertikalen Märkten und Spezialnischen und gibt ihnen die Werkzeuge an die Hand, um den nächsten Schritt zu gehen. Unsere Mission: Ambitionen fördern, Wachstum vorantreiben und Chancen für Europas Software-Ökosystem eröffnen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Die Unternehmen im Everfield-Ökosystem arbeiten dezentral: Sie behalten ihre Teams, Marken und Standorte und konzentrieren sich auf das, was sie am besten können – Produkte entwickeln und Kunden betreuen. Everfield unterstützt mit Talent Acquisition, HR und einem Expertenteam, das zu Finanz- und Operations-Themen berät. Seit der Gründung 2022 ist Everfield in <em>neun</em> Ländern vertreten, Tendenz steigend.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Über SoCom</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Die SoCom Informationssysteme GmbH entwickelt mit rund 45 Mitarbeitenden TIKOS, die führende ERP-Lösung für gewerbliche Wäschereien und Textildienstleister. Mit rund 40 % Marktanteil in der DACH-Region und über 30 Jahren Erfahrung steuern Kunden mit TIKOS ihre gesamte Prozesskette, von der Wäscheannahme über RFID-Tracking bis zur Auslieferung. Seit Oktober 2026 gehört auch die Düchting Software &amp; Consulting GmbH zur SoCom-Familie. SoCom ist Teil des Everfield-Ökosystems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Über die Rolle</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du übernimmst die Verantwortung für unsere gesamte IT: die interne Infrastruktur, die Informationssicherheit und die SoCom Cloud, in der wir TIKOS für unsere Kunden betreiben. Viele dieser Leistungen haben wir bisher extern eingekauft. Jetzt holen wir das Know-how ins Haus – und du stellst die IT so auf, dass sie mit unserem Wachstum, der Integration neuer Unternehmensteile und steigenden regulatorischen Anforderungen Schritt hält.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du bist Gestalter:in und Macher:in zugleich: Du entwickelst die IT-Strategie gemeinsam mit der Geschäftsführung und packst im Tagesgeschäft selbst mit an.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>IT-Verantwortung und Strategie: </strong>Du verantwortest die IT von SoCom ganzheitlich, entwickelst gemeinsam mit der Geschäftsführung eine IT-Roadmap und steuerst das IT-Budget für Hardware, Lizenzen, Cloud und Dienstleister.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Insourcing und Dienstleistersteuerung: </strong>Du überführst bisher extern erbrachte Leistungen – Netzwerk, Firewall, Server, Backup und E-Mail-Security – schrittweise in die eigene Verantwortung. Verbleibende Dienstleister und Verträge steuerst du über klare SLAs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Cloud und Hosting: </strong>Du betreibst die SoCom Cloud, in der wir TIKOS für Kunden hosten, und entwickelst sie weiter. Gemeinsam mit Vertrieb und Support kalkulierst du Hosting-Angebote, verantwortest Verfügbarkeit, Kapazität und Kosten und treibst eine zukunftsfähige Hosting-Architektur voran.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Infrastruktur und Betrieb: </strong>Du verantwortest Server, Netzwerk, Firewall, Backup und Disaster Recovery – am Standort und in der Cloud – sowie Microsoft 365, Endgeräte, Telefonie und Mobilfunk. Monitoring und Patch-Management steuerst du über ein RMM-Tool.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Informationssicherheit und Compliance: </strong>Als interne:r Owner für IT-Security koordinierst du das Schwachstellen- und Incident-Management, arbeitest eng mit dem CISO-Netzwerk von Everfield zusammen und setzt die Anforderungen aus NIS-2, Cyber Resilience Act und DSGVO in der Infrastruktur um.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Integration Düchting: </strong>Du bringst die IT der Düchting Software &amp; Consulting GmbH bis 2027 auf SoCom-Standard und konsolidierst Systeme, Lizenzen und Prozesse.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Dokumentation und Wissenssicherung: </strong>Du baust eine belastbare IT-Dokumentation auf – Systeme, Zugänge, Kosten und Notfallpläne –, damit Wissen im Team geteilt und jederzeit verfügbar ist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Führung und Zusammenarbeit: </strong>Du arbeitest eng mit unserer IT-Administration zusammen und bildest mit ihr ein Team mit gegenseitiger Vertretung. Für Support, R&amp;D, DevOps und Vertrieb bist du die zentrale Ansprechperson für alle IT-Themen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>KI und Digitalisierung: </strong>Du begleitest den sicheren Einsatz von KI-Tools im Unternehmen gemäß der KI-Richtlinie von Everfield und automatisierst interne IT-Prozesse.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Was du mitbringst</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Muss</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Abgeschlossenes Studium (Informatik, Wirtschaftsinformatik o. Ä.) oder Ausbildung zur/zum Fachinformatiker:in mit entsprechender Berufserfahrung</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Mindestens 5 Jahre Erfahrung in der IT-Administration oder im IT-Management, davon mindestens 2 Jahre in verantwortlicher Rolle in einem mittelständischen Unternehmen (ca. 30–250 Mitarbeitende)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Fundierte Praxis mit Windows Server, Active Directory/Entra ID, Microsoft 365, Netzwerken (VLAN, VPN) und Firewalls (z. B. Sophos, Fortinet)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Erfahrung im Betrieb von Cloud- oder Hosting-Infrastruktur (IaaS, z. B. IONOS, Azure, AWS) inklusive Virtualisierung, Backup und Disaster Recovery</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Ausgeprägtes Sicherheitsbewusstsein und praktische Erfahrung im Schwachstellen- und Incident-Management</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Erfahrung in der Steuerung externer IT-Dienstleister sowie im Budget- und Lizenzmanagement</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Hands-on-Mentalität: Du übernimmst Verantwortung und löst Probleme selbst</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Deutsch auf muttersprachlichem Niveau und gute Englischkenntnisse für die Abstimmung im internationalen Everfield-Netzwerk</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kann</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Erfahrung im Hosting von Business-Software für externe Kunden (SLAs, Mandantentrennung)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Kenntnisse in NIS-2, ISO 27001/BSI IT-Grundschutz oder dem Cyber Resilience Act</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Erfahrung mit SQL-Server-Datenbanken und Linux-Systemen</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Erfahrung mit RMM-Tools (z. B. NinjaOne, Datto RMM) und Automatisierung mit PowerShell</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Erfahrung mit IT-Integrationen nach Unternehmenszukäufen</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Kenntnisse im sicheren Einsatz von KI-Tools</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nicht jede:r erfüllt jeden Punkt. Wenn du die Muss-Kriterien weitgehend mitbringst und Lust auf die Aufgabe hast, bewirb dich – wir freuen uns, dich kennenzulernen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bewerbungsprozess</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Erstgespräch (30 Min.) </strong>mit Karolina, Talent Acquisition Partner bei Everfield</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Fachinterview (60 Min.) </strong>mit Stefan Hoffmann, Geschäftsführer SoCom, und Everfield AI Lead</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Finales Gespräch vor Ort in Krumbach (90 Min.) </strong>mit Fallstudie (z. B. ein Insourcing-Plan für einen externen IT-Dienstleister) und Kennenlernen des Teams</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Die Position ist hybrid mit regelmäßiger Präsenz an unserem Standort in Krumbach-Niederraunau</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wir freuen uns auf deine Bewerbung!</strong></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/everfield/it-cloud-manager-krumbach-269315","tags":["SoCom"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany - Krumbach | Hybrid","created_at":1794033627},{"slug":"senior-ai-rd-engineer-model-training-heidelberg-257755","company_name":"Alephalpha","title":"Senior AI R&D Engineer – Model Training  (f/m/d)","description":"<h2>Our Mission</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aleph Alpha is one of the few companies in Europe doing serious foundation model pre-training like our recently released <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://huggingface.co/Aleph-Alpha/Kolibri-1">Kolibri-1 model</a>. Our customers - in finance, manufacturing, public administration - need models that understand German, meet European regulatory requirements, and work reliably in high-stakes settings. We're building that in Heidelberg.<br /></p><h2>Team Culture</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Aleph Alpha, we foster a culture built on ownership, autonomy, and empowerment. Teams and individual contributors are trusted to take responsibility for their work and drive meaningful impact. We maintain a flat organizational structure with efficient, supportive management that enables quick decision-making, open communication, and a strong sense of shared purpose.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe a strong engineering culture is the key to model training success. We like Extreme Programming and favor trunk-based development. We often mob-program, which keeps us aligned and means we always learn from each other.</p><h2></h2><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Senior</strong> <strong>AI R&amp;D Engineer in Model Training (f/m/d),</strong> you will join our model training team in Heidelberg or Berlin. Most of the team is based in Heidelberg. The model training team is building and improving our model training pipeline, which has been used to train Kolibri. </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work across our full stack. Some weeks you might be optimizing how training loads are scheduled on our cluster and making the pipeline more robust and performant so we can iterate faster. Other weeks, you will be enabling large-scale code execution for reinforcement learning. And at other times, you might dig deep into our evaluation codebase to lift inference throughput on evals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">No two days are the same. Things move fast, and your ability to focus and prioritize is what lets you unblock the team day-to-day while designing the high-quality tooling and infrastructure that speeds us up long-term.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're still building out our training pipeline and infrastructure. Some pieces exist, some do not, and you will have real influence on what gets built and how. Your work directly shapes how quickly we can experiment and improve our models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identifying issues and taking initiative is what drives our day-to-day work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working mode, design decisions, priorities are all done in your team together with your team mates. <br />The strongest teams often use highly collaborative techniques, like mob or pair programming.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Due to the highly collaborative nature of our work you are expected to be on-site at least two days a week. If you are in Berlin, you should expect to travel around every second month for a few days to Heidelberg.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are specifically looking to strengthen the Software Engineering in the teams which are research heavy. Major points include improving the maintainability of our code through tests and design &amp; architecture changes.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At its core, you need to be able to dive into a codebase, change the behavior as necessary, and after the change the code should be better tested and easier to understand than before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As such we look for candidates for an understanding of how to design for low coupling and high cohesion paired with the ability to incrementally refactor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with the following technologies is likely to be helpful:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test Driven Development (TDD)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trunk based development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuous integration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Domain Driven Design</p></li></ul></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most of our code is in Python, there is also the occasional Rust codebase.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Large parts of our training pipeline are built on top of Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We do not hire for skills in a particular technology or language, but rather ability to learn and mindset, yet experience with these technologies is a plus.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Become part of an AI revolution!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 days of paid vacation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to a variety of fitness &amp; wellness offerings via <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://wellhub.com/de-de/">Wellhub</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental health support through <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://nilo.health/">nilo.health</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantially subsidized company pension plan for your future security</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Subsidized Germany-wide transportation ticket</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Budget for additional technical equipment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours for better work-life balance and hybrid working model</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.jobrad.org/">JobRad®</a> Bike Lease</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/alephalpha/senior-ai-rd-engineer-model-training-heidelberg-257755","tags":["Research"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Heidelberg","created_at":1794033627},{"slug":"ai-rd-engineer-model-training-heidelberg-20984","company_name":"Alephalpha","title":"AI R&D Engineer – Model Training  (f/m/