, Italy and Greece, with France as your anchor market. Many teams in the region already run NetBird through our open source and self-serve products, and you'll turn that adoption into annual cloud and self-hosted enterprise contracts while opening new mid-market and enterprise accounts. You own the full cycle, from first touch to signed contract and expansion. You'll report to our Head of Sales and work closely with our Solutions Engineers, Marketing and Product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full sales cycle in Southern Europe: prospecting, discovery, demos with a Solutions Engineer, proposals, negotiation and close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn open source and self-serve users into paying annual customers, using product usage signals to find the right accounts and the right moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run outbound into mid-market and enterprise companies that want to replace legacy VPNs such as OpenVPN, Cisco AnyConnect, Fortinet or GlobalProtect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sell to technical buyers, from infrastructure and network engineers to security leads, with a clear story on open source, self-hosting and zero trust.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build relationships with MSPs, integrators and resellers across the region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet customers on site, at conferences and at meetups, and join the team in Berlin for regular offsites.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep your forecast and HubSpot data accurate, and bring regional product and pricing feedback back to the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape messaging for French-speaking markets with Marketing, including compliance and data sovereignty topics such as NIS2, GDPR and SecNumCloud.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a builder role: you'll be the first person dedicated to the region, with a lot 