it, wie sich unsere Abrechnung in Zukunft aufstellt – nicht nur auf dem Papier, sondern auch in der Umsetzung.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dein Talent</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du bringst mindestens 3 Jahre Berufserfahrung in Operations, Prozessmanagement, FinOps, Partnermanagement oder Abrechnungsmanagement mit, idealerweise im Healthcare- oder Tech-Umfeld.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast nachweislich Prozesse von Grund auf aufgebaut und externe Dienstleister gesteuert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du bist proaktiv, übernimmst Ownership, erkennst Verbesserungspotenzial und packst operativ mit an. Dabei kommunizierst du klar und verbindlich – intern wie extern.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du arbeitest analytisch und sehr genau, bist sicher in Google Sheets/Excel und nutzt AI-Tools wie Claude oder ChatGPT selbstverständlich im Arbeitsalltag.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du sprichst Deutsch auf muttersprachlichem Niveau und Englisch mindestens auf B2-Niveau.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Plus</strong>:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung in der Abrechnung mit Pflege-/Krankenkassen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung mit Automatisierung und No-Code-Tools (z. B. Zapier, n8n) oder SQL-Grundkenntnisse</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unser Angebot</strong><br /><br /><strong>⚖️ Fair von Anfang an:</strong> Du bekommst von uns direkt unser bestmögliches Angebot – wir gehen von Anfang an mit der Zahl rein, die woanders erst am Ende einer Verhandlung steht.<br /><br /><strong>🏢 Arbeitsort:</strong> 2 Tage pro Woche mobil arbeiten sowie klimatisiertes Büro mit Spree-Blick mitten in Friedrichshain<br /><br /><strong>📚 Wachstum:</strong> 500€ jährliches Learning &amp; Development-Budget, klarer Career Framework und 360°-Feedback für deine Weiterentwicklung<br /><br /><strong>🤝 Miteinander:</strong> Wir feiern Erfolge gemeinsam bei regelmäßigen Company Events und bei vierteljährlichen Teamevents mit 50€ Budget pro Person für besondere Erlebnisse (z.B. Escape Rooms, Cooking Classes oder Game Shows)<br /><br /><strong>🏖️ Urlaub:</strong> Bis zu 30 Tage Urlaub (nach Start mit 26 im 1. &amp; 28 im 2. Jahr) <br /><br /><strong>🧘 Fitness &amp; Freizeit:</strong> Bis zu 50% Rabatt auf Urban Sports Club, Corporate Benefits, Restaurant-Deals sowie Family &amp; Friends Coupon auf die Patronus Uhr<br /><br /><strong>🚲 Mobilität:</strong> 30% Rabatt aufs Job Ticket sowie vergünstigtes Fahrrad-Leasing<br /><br /><strong>🥤 Verpflegung:</strong> Kostenfreie Softdrinks &amp; Kaffeevollautomat, Müslibar, vierteljährliche Company Brunches sowie wöchentliche Healthy Snacks<br /><br /><strong>💻 Hardware: </strong>Freie Wahl zwischen MacBook und Lenovo <br /><br /><strong>🌍 Impact:</strong> Ein Produkt mit echtem gesellschaftlichem Mehrwert plus ein Volunteering-Tag im Jahr</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Einfach. Sicher. Leben. Mit Patronus.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wir sind mehr als ein Anbieter für intelligente Notruf-Uhren – wir entwickeln Technologien, die Menschen ein selbstbestimmtes Leben ermöglichen: <strong>We create a world where aging is delightful</strong>.<br /><br />Möglich macht das unsere revolutionäre Patronus-Uhr: Auf den ersten Blick nicht als Notruf erkennbar, ermöglicht sie es Nutzer*innen, jederzeit und überall unkompliziert Hilfe zu rufen. Damit sorgen wir für Sicherheit und retten im wahrsten Sinne des Wortes Leben. Sie ist dabei unser Türöffner, um das Leben älterer Menschen, ihrer Angehörigen und Pflegepersonen zu verbessern und das Gesundheitssystem effektiver zu machen. Damit in Zukunft alle Menschen ihr Leben so leben können, wie sie es möchten.<br /><br /><strong>Klingt nach einer perfekten Stelle für dich?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wir freuen uns auf deine Bewerbung und darauf, dich kennenzulernen!</strong><br /><br />Auch wenn du unserem Anforderungsprofil nicht zu 100 % entsprichst, ermutigen wir dich trotzdem, dich bei uns zu bewerben.<br /><br /><em>Patronus ist ein Arbeitgeber, der Chancengleichheit und Vielfalt fördert. Wir bemühen uns, ein freundliches, sicheres und einladendes Umfeld für alle unsere Mitarbeiter*innen zu schaffen, unabhängig von ethnischer Herkunft, Geschlecht, Geschlechtsidentität und -ausdruck, sexueller Orientierung, Einschränkungen und Begabungen jeglicher Art, körperlicher Erscheinung, sozialem Hintergrund, Familienstand, Alter oder Religion (oder deren Fehlen).</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/patronus/senior-operations-manager-abrechnung-pflegekassen-health-tech-german-speaking-berlin-434207","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1794022823},{"slug":"senior-control-systems-engineer-vehicle-dynamics-abstraction-gilching-32929","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Senior Control Systems Engineer – Vehicle Dynamics & Abstraction (m/f/d)","description":"<figure style="text-align:center;"><a target="_blank" href="https://quantum-systems.com/mandrill/"><img style="width:899px" src="https://quantum-systems.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/QS_Press_Word_Press_Ground_Domain.png"></a></figure><p class="Paragraph SCXW18645642 BCX0">We are seeking a Senior Control Systems Engineer to lead the design and execution of robust control layers across a highly diverse fleet of autonomous vehicles. In this role, you will act as the critical boundary layer to the upper autonomy stack. As the industry transitions toward End-to-End driving models, your primary mandate is to ensure that high-level motion commands are executed sensibly and strictly safeguarded at the physical limits of the vehicle.&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW18645642 BCX0">Your designs will address complex, real-world scenarios rather than idealized environments. You will build control architectures that remain robust under severe, highly non-linear real-world conditions. This includes handling sudden tire slip, navigating challenging terrain such as mud, gravel, potholes, and dense vegetation, maintaining stability on steep inclines and side slopes, and delivering predictable tracking despite asymmetric system degradation, such as a damaged mechanics.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What is your Day to Day Mission:</strong></h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW68016270 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW68016270 BCX0"><strong>Control Architecture Abstraction:</strong> Maintain a standardized, platform-agnostic motion command interface that cleanly abstracts underlying mechanical complexity from the planning layers.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW68016270 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW68016270 BCX0"><strong>Multivariable Control &amp; Allocation:</strong> Design and deploy control laws to manage path tracking, velocity execution, and actuator saturation, incorporating data-driven control allocation to dynamically distribute effort across multiple actuators.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW68016270 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW68016270 BCX0"><strong>System Identification &amp; Modeling:</strong> Utilize data-driven system identification techniques to model unknown plant dynamics, latencies, and actuator responses.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW68016270 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW68016270 BCX0"><strong>Pragmatic Simulation &amp; Verification:</strong> Validate control loops rapidly. If filter design and linear/nonlinear analysis indicate a controller will behave, you are empowered to rely on lean, pragmatic subsystem simulations to iterate fast rather than being bottlenecked waiting for massive, full-system high-fidelity simulation runs.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW68016270 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW68016270 BCX0"><strong>Motion Safeguarding:</strong> Ensure that incoming motion commands are dynamically evaluated, bounded, and safeguarded against the physical realities and constraints of the vehicle chassis in real time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong></h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW141234447 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW141234447 BCX0"><strong>Experience:</strong> Proven professional experience developing and deploying real-time closed-loop control systems.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW141234447 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW141234447 BCX0"><strong>Linear &amp; Classical Control Design:</strong> Deep foundational command of classical control theory, including frequency-domain loop-shaping, stability margin analysis (Bode/Nyquist), and standard state-space design methods (LQR/pole-placement).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW141234447 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW141234447 BCX0"><strong>System Identification &amp; Allocation:</strong> Demonstrated experience utilizing system identification methods or empirical frequency response estimation to characterize raw plant dynamics, alongside data-driven control allocation techniques.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW141234447 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW141234447 BCX0"><strong>Nonlinear Control Theory:</strong> Strong theoretical and practical foundation in Differential Geometry as applied to nonlinear systems, specifically utilizing Feedback Linearization and Differential Flatness for exact state transformation.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW141234447 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW141234447 BCX0"><strong>State Estimation:</strong> Proficiency in Kalman Filtering for state estimation under non-holonomic constraints.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW141234447 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW141234447 BCX0"><strong>Implementation &amp; Tooling:</strong> High proficiency in either the MATLAB/Simulink, C++, or Python. The core requirement is your ability to translate complex control logic into clean, deterministic execution ready for real-time environments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4></h4><h4><strong>Your Benefits:&nbsp;</strong></h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Direct impact: </strong>See your contributions rapidly integrated from cutting-edge research into industrialized products, flying in the field within short development cycles.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Culture &amp; Environment: </strong>A dynamic, fast-paced, and collaborative startup environment with flat hierarchies, efficient collaboration, and a strong emphasis on continuous learning opportunities.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Work-life Balance: </strong>We offer flexible work schedules, and 30 days of paid vacation each year to support your personal and professional life.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Lunch Benefit: </strong>We promote healthy eating and the well-being of our employees with a monthly lunch budget.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW113000096 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW113000096 BCX8"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness:</strong> We support your physical well-being with a company-subsidized eGym Wellpass membership, giving you access to thousands of gyms and sports facilities.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/quantum-systems-gmbh/senior-control-systems-engineer-vehicle-dynamics-abstraction-gilching-32929","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Senior manager","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Gilching, Bayern, Germany","created_at":1794022294},{"slug":"senior-payload-integration-engineer-ugv-platforms-munchen-430503","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Senior Payload Integration Engineer - UGV Platforms  (m/f/d)","description":"<figure style="text-align:center;"><a target="_blank" href="https://quantum-systems.com/mandrill/"><img style="width:899px" src="https://quantum-systems.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/QS_Press_Word_Press_Ground_Domain.png"></a></figure><p class="Paragraph SCXW129352738 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;">Join Quantum-Systems and help bring autonomous ground systems into real-world operations. As Senior Payload Integration Engineer, you will own the payload integration across our UGV platforms: the electrical, electronic, and mechanical integration of a wide range of mission payloads into our own Mandrill UGV and partner vehicle platforms. Your goal is a payload-agnostic platform with scalable, reusable interfaces instead of one-off solutions, so we can adapt quickly to evolving mission needs without redesigning the vehicle for every new configuration.<span style="background-color:#C6C6C6">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW129352738 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;">This is a senior individual contributor role with real ownership. You drive the integration architecture end to end, from interface definition through bring-up and commissioning to the point where the complete E/E system is proven to work on the vehicle. You will work at the intersection of vehicle hardware, autonomy and MOSAIC orchestration software, mechanical engineering, 