ute, and software.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW207530262 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0">Drive payload mounting together with internal vehicle teams and external suppliers: brackets, packaging, accessibility, vibration robustness, environmental protection, maintainability, and manufacturability.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0"><strong>Bring-up, Commissioning and Validation</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW207530262 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0">Plan and execute payload bring-up and commissioning on vehicle prototypes and demonstrators: mechanical fitment, electrical integration, software provisioning (flashing, configuration, diagnostics), troubleshooting, and validation up to full system commissioning where the complete E/E system is proven to work.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW207530262 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0">Define acceptance criteria, build and run system-level test setups, automate recurring integration and regression tests with scripts and test tooling, and support field testing.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW207530262 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0">Translate integration findings into design improvements for vehicle and payload interfaces, and feed validated test workflows into our CI and test infrastructure together with the HW integration and SW Factory teams.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW207530262 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0">Work directly with payload suppliers: clarify requirements, review technical documentation, align interface specifications, and drive issue resolution.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration and Documentation</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW207530262 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0">Create clear interface control documents, integration guides, test reports, lessons learned, and reusable standards for future payload integrations.&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW207530262 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW207530262 BCX0">Actively support build-ups, rework, payload installation, and vehicle-level commissioning in the workshop during prototype and customer-specific integration phases.&nbsp;</p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong><br></strong></h4><h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong><br></h4><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW201480477 BCX0">Engineering degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, vehicle systems, or a comparable technical field.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW201480477 BCX0">5+ years of hands-on experience in field robotics, vehicle, or mechatronic system integration; you have brought complex E/E systems to life on real vehicles or machines.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW201480477 BCX0">Strong E/E integration expertise: power distribution, signal interfaces, connectors, wiring harnesses, grounding, shielding, diagnostics, and vehicle-level troubleshooting.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW201480477 BCX0">Hands-on experience with vehicle communication buses (CAN, ideally CAN-FD or automotive Ethernet), including reading and debugging bus traffic during integration.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW201480477 BCX0">Solid mechanical integration understanding: mounting concepts, packaging, tolerances, vibration, environmental robustness, accessibility, and serviceability.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW201480477 BCX0">Practical software skills for integration work: Linux, scripting (e.g. Python or Bash), software provisioning and configuration of embedded devices, and issue tracking tools. You are comfortable automating recurring integration tests.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW201480477 BCX0">Experience defining and running validation setups from ben