ergraph/Mission-and-Core-Beliefs-20fb19e0a0ec80c09646fa9101368bce"><u>Core Beliefs </u></a>and  if you want to make an impact, have your voice heard, and work in a no-BS organization where you can get stuff done, look no further and apply today so we can chat.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h2>ABOUT THE ROLE</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Senior Talent Partner has moved into the Head of People and Talent role, so we're looking for someone to take over day-to-day hiring processes for the whole company. We're growing across every team, and you'll be the person who makes sure each of them gets great people when they need them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-cycle role first. You'll own searches end to end, from shaping the brief with a hiring manager to closing the offer. Roughly half your roles will be in engineering and half in other functions, so one week you're calibrating an engineering loop and the next you're hiring for sales or operations. A lot of the people we want aren't looking, so you'll find many of them yourself.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The other part of the job is building a talent community around WunderGraph. We're an open-source company with a real developer community, and hiring should draw on that. Events, content, memes, a community experiment that might not work: you'll have room to try things, and we'd rather you tried.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">One thing this isn't - a sales role. We don't need someone to push candidates over the line. We need someone who tells our story honestly and specifically enough that the right people lean in and the wrong ones opt out early. That includes the less glamorous parts, like a small distributed team and meetings that stretch into your evening so we can work with the US.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>TEAM INTEGRATION</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to: Head of People and Talent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborates closely with: every hiring manager across engineering and non-engineering teams, plus the CEO, COO, VP of Sales and our engineering principals on key hires</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acts as each hiring manager's partner on a search, not an order-taker: shaping the brief, setting the bar together, and holding the process to it</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>ROLE OBJECTIVES</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are succeeding if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring managers across engineering and non-engineering teams get strong shortlists when they need them, not a quarter later.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regardless of source, the candidates are some of the best talent around, rather than people who happened to apply - and you can recognise the difference.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every search you run has a clear brief, a consistent structured process, and no candidate waiting more than 3 days to hear from us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The people you hire are still here and doing well a year on. We scaled sustainably, not just quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A talent community exists around WunderGraph that didn't before: people who know us, follow what we do, and raise their hand when the right role opens.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates keep telling us ours is the best hiring process they've been through, including the ones we don't hire. You keep it that way as we hire more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring managers trust your judgement enough to change their minds when you push back on a brief, and leadership trusts the plan because your hiring metrics are clear.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our hiring processes are better because you changed them, not just because you ran them.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>ROLE TASKS</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role focuses on, but is not limited to:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Full-cycle recruiting</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running multiple searches at once across engineering and non-engineering teams, from intake to accepted offer, prioritised by urgency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running role kickoffs with hiring managers to agree outcomes, competencies and the interview loop</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writing job profiles and adverts with the People team, tailored to each audience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pre-screening candidates and sharing shortlists with a clear recommendation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinating interviews and running debriefs, with blind scorecards in Ashby before any group discussion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping every candidate updated, with no one waiting more than 3 days to hear from us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing offers and closing candidates honestly, without pressure, ensuring each conversation with the candidates is meaningful and insightful for both us and the candidate.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sourcing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Finding and engaging people who aren't looking, through sourcing, open-source projects, communities, meetups and conferences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Headhunting directly for senior and hard-to-fill roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writing outreach specific enough to each person that they actually reply</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping warm pipelines for roles we hire repeatedly</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholders and reporting</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advising hiring managers on market realities: who's available, what they expect, and what that means for the brief</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping leadership updated with clear hiring metrics and progress</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalating blockers early, with a proposed fix</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Talent community and employer marketing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building a community of people who know WunderGraph before they ever see a job post</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running creative, low-budget activity: events, content, community-led hiring, the odd meme that lands</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working out what worked, and dropping what didn't</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring process</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improving our interview loops, tasks and scorecards, including for technical roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Documenting our recruitment workflows so they don't live in one person's head</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping hiring compliant across the countries we hire in, and handling contracts, background checks and documentation with the People team where needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping our hiring data and Ashby setup useful for planning, not just record-keeping23w</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>ROLE REQUIREMENTS</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've run full-cycle recruiting for both technical and non-technical roles, and can walk through searches you owned from brief to accepted offer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a strong sourcer. You find people who aren't looking, and your outreach gets replies because it's written for the person reading it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You tell a company's story in a way that makes the right candidates lean in: honest, specific, never a hard sell.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You keep several very different searches moving at once without letting candidate experience slip.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work independently and keep things moving when the path isn't clear, without waiting to be told what to do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're based in Europe or the UK and can regularly overlap with US hours. For CET or EEST, that means some later evenings.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus points</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built or redesigned a technical hiring process (the loop, the task, the scorecard), not just run one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built a talent community or run creative employer marketing that led to real hires.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've hired in, or for stakeholders in, the US market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've handled hiring compliance, contracts or background checks across more than one European country.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why WunderGraph?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from wherever you thrive—we’re fully remote and globally distributed. If you're in Miami, come work with us in person! We also provide co-working space options worldwide if needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pick your preferred work hardware</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We focus on getting stuff done, and on having fun whilst doing so: work hard, play hard!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can make a real difference and find lots of opportunities to grow together with us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discretionary PTO: take the time you need to recharge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depending on location, we offer healthcare benefits according to local standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team retreats across the globe</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Note: This is a full-time, fully remote position. We are looking for someone who is available to work during European (CET) business hours.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect your time and interest in WunderGraph. This is why we're aiming to make the process as fast as possible. Here's what you can expect:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">45 min discussion with the hiring manager. Following this, you might receive a small take home assignment related to the role. This is your chance to prove your skill!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete the assignment and review together with hiring manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the founders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture fit call with team members</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process also includes reference and background checks. We aim to respond or provide feedback in 2 or 3 days between each stage of the process. We're usually hiring through Deel as our Employer of Record, except for Germany or Florida where we're hiring directly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">WunderGraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can find out more about our ways of working together here:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/wundergraph/WunderGraph-Public-Handbook-and-Resources-20db19e0a0ec800690cac27c35fadc73"><u>WunderGraph Public Handbook and Resources</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking forward to your application so we can grow together!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: €60 – €75,000</p><ul><li>EMEA • Base salary, depending on experience €60 – €75,000</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/wundergraph/senior-talent-partner-frankfurt-85621","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"EMEA","created_at":1794012012},{"slug":"senior-product-designer-emea-frankfurt-342999","company_name":"Wundergraph","title":"Senior Product Designer EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">WunderGraph is a fast-growing startup, our goal is to bring everybody together to build digital products end-to-end. From interface design to API implementation, we provide the platform to go from sketch to product in a category-defining collaborative experience.  Our North Star is to take the friction out of bringing digital ideas to life, making room for your ideas and productivity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Developers from some of the biggest companies in the world are using WunderGraph to design and streamline their API environments. We raised our Series A ($7.5 million USD) in March 2025, being backed by eBay,  Karma Ventures, and Aspenwood Ventures.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The culture we are creating together is extremely important to us. Read here how we are <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://wundergraph.com/blog/category/culture"><u>Building the Company We Always Wanted to Work In</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We invite everyone that wants to join us to understand our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/wundergraph/Mission-and-Core-Beliefs-20fb19e0a0ec80c09646fa9101368bce"><u>Core Beliefs </u></a>and  if you want to make an impact, have your voice heard, and work in a no-BS organization where you can get stuff done, look no further and apply today so we can chat.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Product Designer at WunderGraph, you are the connection between what our users will find most helpful and what our engineers build. Considering the users also happen to be other developers, this becomes an interesting challenge to think about the Developer Experience as the User Experience. You combine sharp user insight, craft, and pragmatism to deliver experiences that are elegant, usable, and built to scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a wide-reaching role, as design roles at a startup should be. One week you might be running user interviews to shape a new feature; the next, refining our design system or designing a marketing landing page. You ground your work in evidence rather than assumption, partner closely with product and engineering, and turn what you learn about users into a clear, informed UX strategy that guides where we go next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TEAM INTEGRATION</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to the VP of Product; is part of the Product team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aligns closely with the CEO (Product) and Head of Customer Success (customer experience and business impact)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate within the Product team with the Delivery Lead and the Design Engineer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborates cross-functionally with engineering, marketing, product, and customer success</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ROLE OBJECTIVES</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are successful if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of the complete design lifecycle, bridging the gap between initial discovery and final delivery for web and product interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivate an evidence-based UX strategy that leverages user research and data to steer the product's evolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee the growth of a unified and extensible design system that spans both our product and marketing efforts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Convert user insights and organizational objectives into pragmatic, human-centric solutions engineered for long-term scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advocate for excellence in accessibility, responsiveness, and performance as fundamental pillars of your craft.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide mentorship to the team, sharing expertise in research methodologies and design principles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Refine the visual and functional identity of WunderGraph through meticulous and high-impact design work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact high-level product strategy by demonstrating how user-focused decisions drive tangible business impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ROLE TASKS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role focuses on, but is not limited to:</p><h3><strong>Product Design</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and prototype user flows, interfaces, and interactions with scalability in mind.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own design problems end to end. From initial concept through execution and iteration after launch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rapidly produce wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity designs, exploring multiple concepts and iterating quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and evolve our design system and component library, keeping it consistent and maintainable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with engineers on feasibility, quality, and handoff, contributing to technical decisions (and coding where you're comfortable and it helps as a plus, not a requirement).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introduce advanced prototyping, interaction design, and motion practices.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>UX Research &amp; Strategy</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and conduct user research across discovery and validation via user interviews, surveys, usability testing, and competitor analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn ambiguous product questions into decision-grade research that maps to real product and design decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Synthesize findings into clear insights, personas, journey maps, and opportunity areas that the team can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a shared insight repository so learning is reusable, searchable, and available to everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate research into an informed, evolving UX strategy that guides the roadmap and anchors design direction in real user needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advocate for the user in prioritization and roadmap discussions, and define what "better" looks like through clear UX success metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run discovery workshops and share insights so research shows up where decisions are made like in  design reviews, product planning, and standups embedding user knowledge from the get-go.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Web &amp; Brand Experience</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the design and evolution of WunderGraph's web presence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver assets that span product and marketing: landing pages, visuals, campaign graphics, and interactive components.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape and maintain a cohesive style guide, balancing design innovation with consistency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support brand storytelling with motion graphics and interactive elements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ROLE REQUIREMENTS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior-level experience in Product Design or UX/UI Design, with a strong portfolio of shipped work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience planning and running UX research (both generative and evaluative) and turning findings into strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Figma, prototyping tools, and Adobe Creative Suite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong background in UX and interaction design, accessibility, responsive design, and usability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience contributing to or leading design systems and component libraries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable using data and research to inform and defend design decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of front-end technologies (HTML/CSS, JavaScript a plus) enough to collaborate closely with engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication, storytelling, and collaboration skills in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A self-starter who is comfortable with ambiguity and can lead initiatives independently in a fast-moving startup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working 100% remotely in a distributed team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel occasionally for team retreats and workshops.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why WunderGraph?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from wherever you thrive—we’re fully remote and globally distributed. If you're in Miami, come work with us in person! We also provide co-working space options worldwide if needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pick your preferred work hardware</p>