ant-and-Job-Candidate-Privacy-Notice.pdf"><u>Global Applicant and Job Candidate Privacy Notice</u></a>. For US applicants, by submitting your application, you agree to the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://cognition.com/documents/Cognition-Applicant-Arbitration-Agreement.pdf"><u>Applicant Arbitration Agreement</u></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cognition/partner-deployed-engineer-europe-london-167976","tags":["Customer Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794033629},{"slug":"remote-ap-ar-assistant-397527","company_name":"Uforce","title":"AP/AR Assistant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE exists to make aggression unaffordable.<br /><br />Founded in Ukraine and headquartered in London, UFORCE is a defence-technology company with operations across Europe, the United States and Asia.<br /><br />UFORCE builds uncrewed vessels, ground robotics and aircraft, autonomy software, and the command-and-control layer that operates them together. Each platform is deployable on its own, and stronger as part of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an Accounts Payable and Receivable Assistant to keep our day-to-day payables and receivables accurate, timely, and audit-ready. You will own the detail of supplier invoice processing, customer invoicing, and cash allocation, follow our financial controls, and raise blockers early. Your work allows the wider team to move quickly without losing financial discipline.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be part of the Finance team and work closely with budget owners, procurement, commercial teams, and colleagues across the business who supply approvals and billing information. The role suits someone who takes pride in accuracy, is comfortable working to regular deadlines, and knows when to escalate an issue rather than leave it unresolved.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process supplier invoices end to end, including checking that they are complete and approved, coding them correctly, and posting them promptly across the entities you support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise customer invoices promptly once approved billing inputs are received, and keep billing accurate and well documented.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Allocate customer receipts to the correct accounts quickly, and investigate and resolve unidentified payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and complete AP and AR reconciliations by the agreed monthly deadline, supporting a clean and timely month-end close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate differences and unusual items, and escalate anything that remains unexplained to the appropriate owner without delay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the approvals and supporting evidence required for every transaction you handle, so that records are complete for internal review and external audit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review overdue payables and receivables each week, assign an owner and next action to each overdue item, and follow up until it is resolved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Respond to queries from suppliers, customers, and internal colleagues on invoices, payments, and account balances.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow documented procedures and financial controls, and suggest improvements where you see ways to make processes more accurate or efficient.</p></li></ul><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience processing accounts payable and accounts receivable, including reconciliations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A high standard of accuracy and close attention to detail, particularly in coding and data entry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A good understanding of financial controls, with sound judgement about what to approve, query, or escalate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong prioritisation and follow-through, with the ability to meet recurring deadlines and keep many items moving at once.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written and spoken communication, including raising issues promptly and explaining them concisely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of accounting systems and strong spreadsheet skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting month-end close and audit requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working across multiple legal entities or currencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a fast-growing or scaling business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A qualification or part-qualification in accounting or finance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/remote-ap-ar-assistant-397527","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom | Remote","created_at":1794033629},{"slug":"chief-engineer-air-london-98633","company_name":"Uforce","title":"Chief Engineer, Air","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE exists to make aggression unaffordable.<br /><br />Founded in Ukraine and headquartered in London, UFORCE is a defence-technology company with operations across Europe, the United States and Asia.<br /><br />UFORCE builds uncrewed vessels, ground robotics and aircraft, autonomy software, and the command-and-control layer that operates them together. Each platform is deployable on its own, and stronger as part of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE is looking for a <strong>Chief Engineer, Air</strong> to lead the engineering of our Western-facing air platforms and turn operational lessons from Ukraine into reliable, manufacturable products that global customers can test, deploy and reorder.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll own the technical baseline across the air portfolio, initially focusing on Platform N and expanding to other platforms sold outside Ukraine. You’ll work closely with Ukrainian engineering teams to understand the wider Nemesis pipeline, translate field experience into product improvements and build a consistent view of configurations and engineering evidence across the portfolio.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on senior technical leadership role. You’ll stay close to the hardware and the field, build a small engineering team, and bring engineering, manufacturing, supply chain and commercial partners together to deliver products at pace without compromising technical rigor.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is based in the UK and involves regular travel to engineering teams, manufacturing sites, test ranges and customers. Reporting arrangements and travel expectations will be confirmed during the hiring process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you’ll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the air portfolio’s technical baseline.</strong> Establish controlled requirements, configurations, bills of materials and test evidence, starting with Platform N and extending across Western and Ukrainian air platforms. Put clear ownership and practical change control in place.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead end-to-end systems engineering.</strong> Make and coordinate technical decisions across airframe, propulsion, power, avionics, flight control, communications, navigation, payload interfaces, software interfaces and ground systems, bringing in specialists where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve reliability and performance.</strong> Establish a disciplined failure-reporting and corrective-action process, investigate priority field and test issues, and demonstrate improvements against agreed requirements through repeatable testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn operational lessons into product improvements.</strong> Work with Ukrainian engineering and field teams to understand what has worked, capture operator feedback and agree a prioritised design-change roadmap for Western variants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build for repeatable production.</strong> Lead design-for-manufacture reviews and partner with manufacturing teams to release production-ready engineering packages for US and allied sites.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strengthen the supply chain and cost position.</strong> Work with supply-chain and compliance partners to assess component sourcing, qualification, capacity and critical supplier risks. Develop a unit-cost roadmap and evaluate where components and systems should be built across UFORCE locations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support go-to-market and customer delivery.</strong> Partner with Sales and Business Development on customer requirements, priority markets, product positioning and business cases. Provide technical input on configurations, capability claims, pricing, delivery and support assumptions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prepare for trials and launch.</strong> Establish technical readiness gates covering demonstrations, compliance evidence, production readiness and handover to field support. Communicate product capabilities and limitations honestly to customers and test authorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set the direction and build the team.</strong> Work with founders, Ukrainian colleagues and global leadership to develop the air product roadmap. Hire and develop engineers, establish clear ownership and build the practices needed as the function grows.</p></li></ul><h2>Required Skill</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading the design and development of a complete UAS, with personal ownership of system-level technical decisions and demonstrated flight or field outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong systems engineering judgement across airframe, propulsion, power, avionics, flight control, communications, navigation and software interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking an aerial or comparable electromechanical product from prototype into repeatable production, including design for manufacture, configuration control and production testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of investigating field failures, identifying root causes and measurably improving reliability through verified corrective actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience with applicable NDAA / Blue UAS sourcing requirements, restricted componen