m through requirements, architecture, design, integration, verification, production release, and real-world operation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Broad systems judgment across multiple engineering disciplines, with the ability to understand interactions, challenge assumptions, and lead consequential technical trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of materially improving system or product performance using first-principles engineering, structured experimentation, and objective evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience shortening development or upgrade cycles in a high-consequence environment while maintaining appropriate safety, design assurance, configuration control, and verification.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking a complex product from prototype or low-volume development into repeatable production, or materially improving reliability, quality, yield, maintainability, cost, or throughput.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The technical credibility to lead highly capable specialists without needing to be the deepest expert in every discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A leadership style that develops engineers, creates clear ownership, encourages constructive challenge, and treats failed hypotheses as a source of learning rather than blame.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating in a fast-moving, globally distributed environment with incomplete structure, constrained resources, and rapidly changing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to work directly with engineers, factories, test teams, deployed personnel, customers, and operators wherever the most important technical problem exists.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing unmanned, autonomous, robotic, aerospace, maritime, defense, or other safety- or mission-critical systems.</p></l