fine intended outcomes and acceptance criteria while keeping requirements development collaborative and iterative.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve product and programme control across hardware and software, including configuration visibility, versioning, dependencies, readiness, and lifecycle decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage directly in relevant customer meetings, demonstrations, trials, testing, deployments, factory activity, and field operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enter the detail and personally unblock priority products or programmes when execution is at risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build only the minimum Product organisation required, hiring high-leverage leaders and individual contributors who strengthen technical-operational judgment and execution.</p></li></ul><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive product leadership experience in defence technology, robotics, autonomous systems, aerospace, advanced hardware, industrial technology, or another integrated hardware–software environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning product strategy and cross-product decisions across multiple products, platforms, markets, or operating regions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of rapidly learning technically complex products and working directly with engineers, factories, customers, operators, testing teams, deployments, or field operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading urgent, cross-functional programmes and resolving execution conflicts across functions, sites, or geographies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong judgment in balancing common platform capabilities with deliberate customer-, mission-, or market-specific development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to make hard prioritisation and capacity decisions with incomplete information—and clearly explain what should accelerate, pause, stop, or remain separate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience connecting strategic R&amp;D, operational need, customer opportunity, technical feasibility, manufacturing capacity, and commercial value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The technical credibility to challenge product and system assumptions without displacing Engineering’s ownership of architecture, standards, and technical delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A history of partnering effectively with senior hardware, software, manufacturing, delivery, and commercial leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct credibility with demanding customers and operators, grounded in first-hand engagement and evidence rather than reports alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A low-ego, highly accountable leadership style and a willingness to get into the detail when the mission requires it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating amid urgency, ambiguity, changing priorities, and incomplete data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to operate from CEO and board-level portfolio decisions through to detailed product and programme intervention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in London or willing to relocate, with the ability to travel regularly to UFORCE engineering, manufacturing, customer, and field locations and engage meaningfully with Ukraine-related teams and priorities.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with uncrewed systems, autonomy, command-and-control software, defence platforms, contested operations, or other mission-critical systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience reconciling product and resource priorities across countries, development sites, factories, customer environments, and markets at different levels of maturity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience converting strategic R&amp;D or customer-funded development into fielded, supported products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to government procurement, export and regulatory constraints, interoperability requirements, and deployment into allied defence ecosystems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing product configuration, versioning, supportability, and lifecycle complexity across integrated hardware–software systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of preserving rapid execution while introducing only the minimum structure required for visibility, accountability, and sound decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or upgrading a lean product organisation without turning Product into a process-heavy intermediary between users and technical teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/chief-product-officer-london-235792","tags":["C-Suite"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom - London","created_at":1794033629},{"slug":"enterprise-migrations-practice-area-lead-london-326257","company_name":"Infinite Lambda","title":"Enterprise Migrations Practice Area Lead","description":"<h2><strong>About us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Infinite Lambda is a data and AI consultancy that helps the world’s leading companies become data-first. We design and build modern, cloud-native data platforms, and we help our clients turn them into real business value with AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re one of Europe’s fastest-growing consultancies, and we’re now a global team across three regions. Headquartered in London, we have engineers and consultants in the United States, the UK, France, Italy, Hungary, Slovakia, Romania, Bulgaria, Vietnam and Singapore. We’re also building new teams in Brazil, Argentina and Chile.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to bring exceptional people together to make an impact where technology meets sustainable growth. You’ll work alongside experts in dbt, Snowflake and the wider modern data stack on complex, meaningful projects, in a culture built on curiosity, experimentation and continuous learning.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a diverse team, and we want everyone to feel comfortable being themselves at work. If you want to grow fast, learn constantly and help shape where we go next, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every enterprise wants to be AI-ready, and most are held back by legacy data estates built over decades. As Enterprise Migrations Practice Area Lead, you’ll own how Infinite Lambda solves that problem: moving the world’s largest organisations off Informatica, Talend, SSIS/SQL Server, DataStage, stored procedures and, increasingly, SAS and Alteryx, onto modern platforms ready for AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enterprise migrations are a core pillar of our growth strategy, and this role sets the standard for how we deliver them globally. The practice spans the full migration lifecycle:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Assess:</strong> Estate discovery, feasibility analysis and migration strategy, ending in a fixed-cost, fixed-timeline proposal that gives clients certainty from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Convert:</strong> Automated code conversion with Flowline, our proprietary product, which combines deterministic and LLM-assisted methods. This stage also covers refactoring, optimisation and a first-pass ontology that lays the foundation for AI use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Validate:</strong> Reconciliation architecture and row-level sign-off, so every migration is provably correct.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">The first part is <strong>delivery excellence that compounds</strong>. You’ll make sure every migration we deliver is better than the last. That means defining the standards, building the playbooks and reusable assets, and turning the lessons from each strategic engagement into capability across the practice. You’ll also develop the engineers and leads who carry that standard across AMER, EMEA and APAC.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The second part is <strong>commercial impact</strong>. You’ll turn delivery quality into a competitive edge: faster delivery, sharper scoping and pricing, and healthy margins you can measure and report on. Working closely with Sales and Solution Engineering, you’ll shape the offer that makes Infinite Lambda the obvious choice for enterprise migration, anywhere in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1. Practice and standards</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the person engineers, sales and clients ask when a migration question is hard: what to migrate first, what to refactor and what to move as is, and how to resolve conflicting logic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the migration standard for Assess, Convert and Validate. This covers reference architectures, sequencing, reconciliation and stage-gate checklists, and what we won’t do. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure Fast and Deep Discovery produce a defensible estimate, a dependency map and early red flags before we commit to a fixed price.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hold the same quality bar in every region: conversion quality, reconciliation sign-off and post-go-live incidents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the practice up to date as Flowline, the source parsers and the target platforms change (Snowflake, Databricks, BigQuery, Iceberg).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2. Knowledge, IP and the asset catalogue</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join engagements at scoping and agree what each strategic migration should leave behind (patterns, decisions, failure modes, measurements) and who will capture it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capture lessons at wave checkpoints, and close each engagement with a review of what worked, what didn’t, and what should change in the standard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide which lessons become reusable assets and which stay one-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring field requirements and recurring challanges to the Flowline product team, and move proven assets into Product &amp; Services.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3. People and enablement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build a global bench of migration specialists.</strong> Develop engineers across AMER, EMEA and APAC into a team that can deliver migration waves to our standard, independently and at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the path from practitioner to leader.</strong> Design and run the progression that takes engineers from dbt and Snowflake foundations, through Flowline accreditation and deep expertise in a legacy source system, to owning delivery waves and ultimately leading client assessments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn what we know into how we work.</strong> Make our accelerators and existing assets visible and reusable across every team, so each engagement starts from our best work rather than a blank page.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>4. Commercial</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure live engagements actually use the practice’s accelerators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help Sales and Sales Engineers scope, estimate and price from measured delivery speed, so the client pays for the acceleration instead of getting it for free.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make the commercial case for the practice in proposals, extensions and new scope. This includes turning Discovery engagements into migrations and expanding into BI and semantic-layer work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5. Partners and internal work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the technical lead in joint pursuits with Snowflake, Databricks, dbt and Fivetran, and feed what we learn in delivery into joint go-to-market, certifications and co-marketing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write interview material and run technical interviews for migration roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Present the practice’s work inside the company and, where it makes sense, at external events and in case studies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership at a strategic level.</strong> You take full accountability for outcomes, not just tasks. You’ve owned a practice, a service line or a major programme end to end (its direction, quality, people and commercial results), and you’re comfortable making the calls that shape how a business delivers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enterprise migration experience at scale.</strong> You have a track record of leading large, complex migrations off legacy platforms such as Informatica, Talend, Oracle, SSIS or DataStage, and you know where these programmes tend to go wrong.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Depth across both ends of the migration.</strong> You have hands-on knowledge of legacy source systems and modern platforms (Snowflake, Databricks, BigQuery, Iceberg, dbt, Fivetran), plus a structured approach to assessment, conversion and validation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A builder of repeatable delivery.</strong> You’ve defined reference architectures, sequencing frameworks and quality gates, and built libraries of reusable assets and accelerators that teams actually use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A multiplier of talent.</strong> You’ve developed engineering teams across regions through mentoring, structured skill pathways and accreditation, and you’ve raised the bar for how those teams deliver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Credibility with clients and partners.</strong> You can lead discovery sessions with senior client stakeholders, act as the technical lead in joint pursuits with partners such as Snowflake and Databricks, and assess engineering talent in interviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial awareness.</strong> You understand how delivery choices affect scoping, pricing and margin, and you enjoy working with Sales to win the right work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Line management &amp; how you will be supported</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your line manager is the Chief Customer Success Officer, who is accountable for your direction, the practice charter and the review of your objectives. Strategic direction will be consulted with CTO and Head of Engineering.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why join Infinite Lambda</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We support your growth</strong> with dedicated learning time, access to top-notch resources and a knowledge-sharing culture;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You work autonomously here</strong> in a wholesome environment and get as much paid holiday as you need;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The projects are diverse</strong> and give you plenty of opportunity to experiment with new tech;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The benefits are plenty</strong>, with work-from-home budget, a company MacBook and more on the list.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>▶ ▶ </strong>Submit your <strong>CV in English in PDF</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>▶ ▶ </strong>Mind that as we are an international team, internal communication is in English.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>▶ ▶ </strong>To ensure legislative compliance, applicants may be asked to provide up-to-date proof of a clean criminal record. Examples of said proof include extract n°3 of the Criminal Record (France), Büntetlen előélet (Hungary), Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check (UK), an extract from the Criminal Register (Slovakia), or a country-specific equivalent. Providing proof of a clean criminal record is the final step in the hiring process and will only be requested should the applicant accept an offer from Infinite Lambda.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Infinite Lambda is an equal opportunity employer. Our inclusive culture celebrates diversity and treats everyone with dignity and respect. Accordingly, our selection process will never discriminate against applicants on the grounds of any characteristics, such as disability, age, gender, sexual orientation, family status, race, faith or other.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: £8K – £11K per month • Offers Commission</p><ul><li> • OTE £8K – £11K per month • Offers Commission</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/infinite-lambda/enterprise-migrations-practice-area-lead-london-326257","tags":["