&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/graphcore/staff-data-analyst-bristol-420434","tags":["Data & Strategic Projects"],"job_types":[],"location":"Bristol","created_at":1794023716},{"slug":"senior-network-operations-engineer-bristol-471735","company_name":"Graphcore","title":"Senior Network Operations Engineer","description":"&lt;h2&gt;About the job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Turn complex network faults into lasting fixes, and make new services ready for reliable operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Network Operations Engineer in Bristol, UK, you’ll keep Graphcore’s networks reliable and secure. This full-time role spans the network lifecycle, from shaping operational requirements to resolving complex incidents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your improvements will reduce downtime and manual errors across new and existing services. You’ll help colleagues operate services confidently, with practical runbooks and recovery procedures ready when problems arise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll troubleshoot routing and firewalls, improve monitoring and automate routine operations. You’ll also support upgrades and deployments through testing, controlled changes and clear handovers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your scope includes AWS networking, Cisco Software-Defined Access and SD-WAN across cloud and on-premises environments. Occasional travel to remote data centres and offices will involve installations, troubleshooting and hands-on support.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a supportive, multidisciplinary IT infrastructure team that works closely together and regularly shares knowledge. With new projects ahead, you’ll bring operational experience into network designs alongside architects and project teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior escalation point, you’ll own complex incidents through to resolution. You’ll use monitoring evidence and recurring incident trends to prioritise reliability improvements.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AWS networking, Cisco Software-Defined Access (SDA) or SD-WAN experience would be particularly valuable, but is not essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least five years’ hands-on network engineering experience, focused on production support, with certification in a major networking platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong practical knowledge of large-scale L2/L3 networks, including BGP, OSPF, switching, routing and resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting centrally controlled Wi-Fi, such as Cisco Meraki or Aruba, and resolving connectivity and performance issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and troubleshooting centralised firewalls, including rulesets, NAT and VPNs, plus familiarity with open-source products such as pfSense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on use of Ansible, Python or similar tools to automate operations and manage network configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence-led troubleshooting using monitoring, packet captures and logs, alongside clear communication, documentation and sound judgement during incidents.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible working:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous leave:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement planning support:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Up to 5% matched pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phantom equity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peace of mind protection:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Electric Vehicle Scheme:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Choose an electric vehicle and lease it through salary sacrifice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme and dental cover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Access to controlled technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some roles at Graphcore involve access to technology subject to U.S. export control regulations. Depending on the role, we may need to assess whether export authorisation is required, taking account of factors such as work location, citizenship and immigration status. Where authorisation is required, this may affect whether or when you can start the role. We’ll explain any relevant requirements during the recruitment process.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply to join Graphcore in Bristol and turn your network operations expertise into more reliable services.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/graphcore/senior-network-operations-engineer-bristol-471735","tags":["IT Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Bristol","created_at":1794023716},{"slug":"senior-platform-engineer-london-406010","company_name":"Fanaticsfbg","title":"Senior Platform Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.organization-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About the Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launched in 2021, Fanatics Betting and Gaming is the online and retail sports betting subsidiary of Fanatics, a global digital sports platform. The Fanatics Sportsbook is available to 95% of the addressable online sports bettor market in the U.S. Fanatics Casino is currently available online in Michigan, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and West Virginia. Fanatics Betting and Gaming operates twenty-two retail sports betting locations, including the only sportsbook inside an NFL stadium at Northwest Stadium. Fanatics Betting and Gaming is headquartered in New York with offices in Denver, Leeds and Dublin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming (FBG) is seeking a Senior Platform Engineer to join our Platform Engineering team. This role will sit in either our Runtime/Compute or the Developer Experience/CICD squad.&lt;br&gt;As a Senior Platform Engineer, you will work across cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes platforms, CI/CD systems, and internal developer tooling. You will work closely with Product Engineering, Security, Infrastructure IT, and other platform teams to build, enhance, and support our developer platform. You will help define standards and best practices, and act as a force multiplier for engineering teams by improving reliability, scalability, and developer productivity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and deliver medium-to-large platform projects from implementation through &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain internal platform services and tooling that improve developer experience and delivery velocity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with application teams to unblock delivery and align platform capabilities with developer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cloud cost efficiency and optimization across our cloud and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve operational excellence through observability, automation, and incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help evolve CI/CD pipelines and GitOps-based workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior engineers through code reviews and knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call rotations and incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of experience in platform, infrastructure, DevOps, or software engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Python and Java. Familiarity with Kotlin, Go a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Kubernetes and container orchestration knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven CI/CD and GitOps experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as Code expertise (Terraform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong AWS and cloud-native experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating distributed, high-availability systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mindset and ability to deliver defined projects independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and strong collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with internal developer platforms or tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to regulated or high-availability environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend development experience (Java, Python, Go, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with observability and reliability engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Platform Engineering at FBG&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platform Engineering at FBG operates with a product-first mindset. Our mission is to empower developers with reliable, scalable, and intuitive platforms that accelerate innovation and delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Across Regions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role operates in a globally distributed environment, working closely with teams across the UK, Ireland, and the United States. Strong communication, time zone coordination, and shared ownership are essential for success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Periodic travel to the United States is expected for offsites, planning sessions, and collaboration. Occasional travel within the UK and Ireland may also be required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not sure if you check every box?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe great engineers come from all kinds of backgrounds. We value &lt;strong&gt;impact, technical leadership, and a growth mindset&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;just as much as specific tool experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, we do not offer sponsorship and you do need to be living in the UK or Ireland to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, your interview and onboarding experience may include in-person components, such as onsite interviews or Launching into Better: LIVE—a multi-day cultural immersion in New York City for full-time, non-seasonal hires. These sessions are designed to build connection and bring our culture to life, though specific travel and participation requirements will be confirmed based on your role and location. Your recruiter will provide clear guidance at each stage of the process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fanaticsfbg/senior-platform-engineer-london-406010","tags":["Gaming - Core Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1794023716},{"slug":"head-of-people-paris-30876","company_name":"Scoreplay","title":"Head of People","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">ScorePlay is the AI-powered media infrastructure for sports, built to automate the content operations behind the world's biggest sports organizations. We work with <strong>300+ leagues, competitions, teams and broadcasters</strong> – including Ligue 1 and Premier League clubs, NBA and NFL teams, the Tour de France, the Australian Open, and leading bodies like UEFA and FIBA – helping them turn every moment on and off the field<strong> into high-value, structured content</strong>. Our platform brings all their media into one place and makes it effortless to find, edit and share in seconds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded in 2021</strong>, we’re a <strong>50-person</strong> team based between <strong>New York </strong>and <strong>Paris</strong>, growing <strong>2x year over year</strong> with 98% retention. We’ve raised <strong>$20M+ </strong>from top investors including Alexis Ohanian and Harry Stebbing’s 20VC and elite athletes like Kevin Durant, Raphaël Varane, Mario Götze, Nico Rosberg and Giannis Antetokounmpo.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re <strong>passionate about sports</strong> and thrive in <strong>fast-paced environments</strong> - and you want to help shape how the next generation of fans experience sports, you’re in the right place. We’re on track to become the <strong>global leader in sports media</strong>, and this is definitely the <strong>best time to join our adventure</strong>. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our <strong>Head of People</strong>, you’ll own everything related to our growing workforce (65 people today). Compensation, leveling, performance, org design: most of it exists today and yours, and it’s yours to upgrade to make sure it remains best-in-class as we scale. You’ll lead a lean team across Talent Acquisition and Talent Development (2 people for now), work directly with the CEO and Head of Ops, and have a real say in how ScorePlay scales internationally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s also a rare chance to answer a question most People leaders are only starting to ask: what does a high-performing company look like when AI changes roles, team sizes and what we hire for?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on builder role. You’ll design the frameworks yourself, make decisions with data and ship them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organizational design &amp; workforce planning:</strong> Design organizational structure, spans, team composition, and headcount plans as we scale, including how AI changes roles, team sizes, and what we hire for.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance, leveling &amp; talent management:</strong> Build consistent leveling and performance frameworks across functions. Oversee performance cycles and calibration, and own talent reviews, succession planning, and the resolution of legacy leveling inconsistencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation, equity &amp; benefits:</strong> Build competitive, internally consistent compensation bands, equity frameworks, and regional benefits. Own compensation benchmarking, offer governance, and compensation cost discipline, with particular attention to US-market competitiveness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring strategy &amp; talent standards:</strong> Define hiring priorities, workforce needs, and senior hiring, and set a consistently high talent bar, including AI fluency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-performer retention &amp; growth:</strong> Identify and retain top talent, build meaningful career paths, and own succession and development plans. Monitor regretted attrition and address systemic retention risks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manager effectiveness:</strong> Equip managers to hire, develop, evaluate, and retain strong teams. Set practical management standards and oversee manager development, with clear accountability for performance and people decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Culture &amp; organizational health:</strong> Maintain a cohesive, high-performance culture across regions and hybrid teams. Identify and address organizational friction, engagement risks, and gaps in accountability or collaboration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People analytics &amp; governance:</strong> Define clear People KPIs, review cadence, and decision frameworks. Lead strategic employment-structure decisions, including entity/EOR considerations, in partnership with Finance and Legal.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People function leadership:</strong> Lead and develop the People team, ensuring strong execution of recruiting, employee lifecycle, employee relations, compliance, and HR operations through the team and appropriate external experts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience building People programs in high-growth tech companies</strong>, ideally with 8+ years of progressive experience across People Operations, People Strategy, HRBP, or related roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven ability to design and implement People frameworks</strong>, in at least two of the following areas: compensation and job leveling, performance management and calibration, talent development, or organizational design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong analytical and business judgment</strong>, with the ability to use data to diagnose organizational problems, evaluate trade-offs, and develop practical recommendations that balance employee experience, performance, and financial discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A first managerial experience required</strong>, having led and developed at least a small People or HR team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfort operating hands-on in a lean, fast-moving organization</strong>, building practical first versions of processes and systems rather than relying on large teams or extensive external support.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Why ScorePlay?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join at a pivotal moment:</strong> the V1s are live and working well, and now we’re building the next version together as we scale fast</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A global People agenda:</strong> teams in Paris, New York and across Europe, with US and European comp, employment and culture questions on your desk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real influence:</strong> you’ll work with the CEO and Head of Ops and bring People expertise into the decisions that shape the company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A high bar:</strong> the goal is to have the best possible person in every seat, and you set the standard for what that means.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We know many people hesitate to apply if they don’t meet every single requirement on a job description. If you’re interested in ScorePlay but not sure you tick all the boxes, we’d still love to hear from you, this could be the start of a great long-term collaboration.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/scoreplay/head-of-people-paris-30876","tags":["G&A"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris office","created_at":1794033630},{"slug":"talent-acquisition-manager-paris-45892","company_name":"Scoreplay","title":"Talent Acquisition Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">ScorePlay is the AI-powered media infrastructure for sports, built to automate the content operations behind the world's biggest sports organizations. We work with <strong>300+ leagues, competitions, teams and broadcasters</strong> – including Ligue 1 and Premier League clubs, NBA and NFL teams, the Tour de France, the Australian Open, and leading bodies like UEFA and FIBA – helping them turn every moment on and off the field<strong> into high-value, structured content</strong>. Our platform brings all their media into one place and makes it effortless to find, edit and share in seconds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded in 2021</strong>, we’re a <strong>50-person</strong> team based between <strong>New York </strong>and <strong>Paris</strong>, growing <strong>2x year over year</strong> with 98% retention. We’ve raised <strong>$20M+ </strong>from top investors including Alexis Ohanian and Harry Stebbing’s 20VC and elite athletes like Kevin Durant, Raphaël Varane, Mario Götze, Nico Rosberg and Giannis Antetokounmpo.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re <strong>passionate about sports</strong> and thrive in <strong>fast-paced environments</strong> - and you want to help shape how the next generation of fans experience sports, you’re in the right place. We’re on track to become the <strong>global leader in sport