asionally co-hosted with partners and industry bodies, which means co-building the format, splitting the cost, and sharing the audience. We measure ourselves on meetings and pipeline, not on badge scans.</p><h2><strong>Your Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own Pelico's event growth engine end-to-end, turning field events into a measurable, efficient source of qualified pipeline and customer engagement.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Decide what we do and what we stop:</strong> You own the portfolio—which events we commit to, which we drop, and which formats get more budget next year. This is the heart of the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the event portfolio from strategy and prioritization through delivery, follow-up, and post-event review:</strong> That covers trade shows, webinars, executive dinners, roundtables, as well as Pelico-hosted, customer, and partner events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tie every event to a commercial outcome:</strong> For each event, you'll define the target accounts and audiences, the meeting and pipeline goals, and the metrics that matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run delivery and budget with discipline:</strong> You'll set clear timelines, owners, and vendor plans, keeping spend under control across many activities at once.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get Sales and BDRs committed:</strong> No event goes ahead without Sales ownership, a prospecting plan, pre-booked meetings, and a named follow-up owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make results visible:</strong> You'll set up reliable lead capture and HubSpot tracking so leads, meetings, opportunities, and costs can be tracked for every event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn events into content:</strong> Speaker and customer interviews, event films, social coverage, and approvals with appearing customers—coordinated with team members who produce it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expect travel:</strong> Up to 3 trips per quarter, including on-site setup days.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your Impact</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Field events become a measurable contributor to pipeline, meetings, and MQLs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Budget moves toward the formats that work—scaling efficient levers like webinars and challenging underperforming formats before investing in them again.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A repeatable event playbook (targeting, execution, lead capture, follow-up, and post-event review) is published and used across Marketing, Sales, and BDRs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pelico is seen as the premier enterprise B2B player in its category: executives want to attend Pelico events and return for the next one.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on ownership role. You set the strategy, run the execution yourself, and answer for the results.</p><h2><strong>You'll need:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience owning a multi-format B2B SaaS/tech event portfolio end-to-end: strategy, delivery, follow-up, and review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A commercial mindset. You choose events for named audiences and business goals, not for prestige or attendance, and you can explain your go/no-go trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong budget and ROI discipline, with hands-on use of metrics like cost per MQL and cost per meeting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience aligning Sales and BDR teams on event goals, ownership, and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience co-building events with partners: agreeing on the format, splitting costs, and keeping both brands served.</p></li>