ine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an intermediate-level engineering role, working closely with and under the technical guidance of our Senior Welding Specialist Engineer. You will support electron beam welding (EBW) for our new thruster, laser-welding activities for a high-thrust engine and participate on the manufacturing of the orbital welding for the our Nyx capsule propulsion. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will bring practical knowledge and you will work with design, manufacturing, quality and production teams to turn robust welding requirements into repeatable, well-documented manufacturing processes.<br /></p><h2><br /><strong>What you will do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the development, implementation and continuous improvement of EBW processes for the new thruster and laser-welding processes for our high-thrust engine.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support orbital welding activities (being a qualified welder and support non conformance management).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft, review and maintain Welding Procedure Specifications (WPS) and related welding documentation; support procedure qualification and qualification records in accordance with applicable NASA requirements and program flow-downs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the assessment of weldability, joint design and manufacturing risks, working with design and manufacturing engineering colleagues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and maintain clear welding documentation, including process records, qualification evidence and traceability information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help investigate welding non-conformities and manufacturing issues, support root-cause analysis, and follow corrective actions through to closure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with qualified welding operators and production teams to ensure that approved procedures ar