aking technology accessible for all. We believe in a world where users, creators and enterprises manage their value with ownership and freedom. Our curiosity drives us to innovate, empowering individuals on a global scale. We believe change is constant and our team moves forward as one, with a culture of problem-solving where every employee is empowered and supported to challenge tradition and create solutions. Our mission is simple: to make self-custody accessible and give people the keys to their own financial futures. If you want to make a true impact, we want you to join us at Ledger.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Ledger, we’re proud to be the global platform for digital assets and Web3, with over 20% of the world’s crypto assets secured through our Ledger devices. With our headquarters in Paris, and offices in Vierzon, Grenoble, Montpellier, London, Portland, Geneva, Zurich and Central Singapore, we have a team of around 600 professionals developing a variety of products and services to enable individuals and companies to securely buy, store, swap, grow and manage crypto assets – including the Ledger hardware wallets line with more than 7.5 millions units already sold in 200 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Consolidation team, part of Finance (Accounting &amp; Consolidation), prepares the Group’s IFRS consolidated financial statements across multiple international legal entities. The team is moving its consolidation EPM tool from SAP BFC (ViaReport C&amp;R) to Amelkis EPM, with a go-live targeted for Q1 2027, while preparing the 2026 annual closing. The intern supports both work streams and reports to the Consolidation Director.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>Annual consolidation closing (2026)</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the preparation of the Group’s IFRS consolidated financial statements across multiple legal entities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with intercompany reconciliation and eliminations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process consolidation adjustments and review reporting packages submitted by subsidiaries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Liaise with subsidiary finance teams to collect, control and consolidate reporting packages</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support ad hoc analyses requested during the annual audit</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>EPM tool migration (SAP BFC to Amelkis EPM)</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to data migration, configuration and testing workshops for the new Amelkis consolidation/EPM tool</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in the “double run” phase to ensure data accuracy between the legacy and new systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help document consolidation processes and procedures throughout the tool transition</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s-level student (Bac+4/5) in Accounting, Finance or Audit (DSCG, Master CCA, business or engineering school), looking for a gap year (césure) or an end-of-studies internship</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First experience with, or strong interest in, consolidation and IFRS (previous internship, audit firm exposure or dedicated coursework)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with large data sets and advanced Excel functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity for finance systems and tools (EPM, SAP BFC, Amelkis EPM) is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English and French (the team reports bilin