nt manager. Once the plant manager is convinced, you get to the COO. This is what you'll do:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the deployment:</strong> You're the person who makes sure go-live happens on time and the customer's team knows how to use it. You handle the onboarding, the training, and the change management that gets a new platform embedded into daily operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn shopfloor problems into business cases:</strong> An operator tells you yield drops on line 3 every Tuesday night. You figure out why, quantify what it costs, and build the case for the next deployment. You're as comfortable talking to a process engineer as you are presenting to a VP of Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive expansion:</strong> You know which teams in the account haven't seen Ethon yet, which problems are still unsolved, and what it takes to get the next use case signed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be on-site:</strong> You're in factories. The insights that matter don't come from email chains and slides, they come from being on the floor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feed the product:</strong> You're closest to what customers actually need. You bring that signal back to Engineering and Product and you help us build something better.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work with the team:</strong> GTM &amp; Sales brings the logo with your help as a trustworthy industry expert, you take it from there. You work tightly with Engineering on delivery and with the commercial team on expansion opportunities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT DO YOU NEED TO BRING?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The best people in this seat combine strategic thinking with the willingness to get their hands dirty on a shopfloor. We can teach you our product. We can't teach you to care about how things get made, or to push hard when a deployment is stuck.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're technically sharp enough to understand a production process and commercially minded enough to turn a pain point into a business case</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 3-5 years of experience in something demanding: consulting, enterprise tech deployment, or a career on the shopfloor</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know how to manage complex stakeholder environments, from shopfloor operators to C-suite sponsors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've run change management or adoption programs and know what it takes to get people to actually use new tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a builder mindset: when something isn't working, your instinct is to fix it rather than escalate it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're open to travel 30-50% of the time</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is how we'll set you up in your first six months:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 1-2:</strong> Learn about product, customers, and how our best deployments get done. You shadow live accounts, learn the platform end-to-end, and expand your understanding of how manufacturers think. You start working on your first account.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 3-4:</strong> You own delivery for one or more accounts, with support from the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Months 5-6:</strong> Full ownership of one or more customers. You're running deployments, driving expansion conversations, and your first upsell is in motion.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Great fits tend to come from backgrounds like:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deployment, implementation, or customer success at high-growth industrial tech companies (e.g., Palantir, c3ai, Rockwell, Siemens Digital Indus