s corporate Process Safety Management (PSM) framework as part of the Integrated Management System.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish and embed process safety standards and procedures across current and future projects, including construction, commissioning, start-up and operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure compliance with SEVESO III requirements and support the Major Accident Prevention Policy, Safety Reports, regulatory inspections and audits.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Govern key process safety activities, including HAZOP, LOPA, QRA and Management of Change (MOC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and monitor process safety KPIs and barrier management to strengthen risk control and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead process safety audits, incident learning and improvement initiatives across projects and assets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build process safety capability across the organization through training, guidance and functional leadership for Engineering, Projects, Operations, Maintenance and contractors.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a growing company in a rapidly evolving industry, we are looking for people who embrace change and are motivated to actively contribute to building and scaling our business. You are someone who feels comfortable in an entrepreneurial environment, takes ownership, and thrives when things are still developing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine deep technical expertise with the ability to turn complex regulatory and risk-management requirements into practical standards. Structured and strategic in your approach, you are also willing to work hands-on to move implementation forward. You communicate clearly, make risk-based decisions, and can influence senior stakeholders without relying on formal authority.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p>