<li>Giving back to the community by contributing to open-source software, contributing to our blog, participating in working groups, and stewarding conferences.</li>
</ul>
</div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tweag-by-modus-create/senior-bazel-engineer-netherlands-377403","tags":[],"job_types":[],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1793990727},{"slug":"international-expansion-netherlands-268798","company_name":"Axle Careers","title":"International Expansion - Netherlands","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At Axle Energy, we’re building the infrastructure that will underpin the decarbonised energy system. Our software moves energy usage to times when electricity is cheap and green, by controlling vehicle charging, heating systems, and home batteries. We control hundreds of thousands of energy assets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building in a legacy industry and moving gigawatt-hours of electrons in the real world, but we operate at lightning speed, and we’re growing the team to meet customer demand.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re proud to be supported by world-leading investors, including Energize Capital and Accel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read more about what we’re building <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.axle.energy/blog/analysis/power-of-the-home"><strong><u>here</u></strong></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’re looking for a commercially sharp, highly autonomous operator to drive Axle’s commercial success in the Dutch market.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Axle has quickly become the leader in our operational markets, and we’re now looking to expand our reach internationally. Our goal is to become the go-to platform for energy flexibility globally, and we’re hiring the person to make that happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will assess Axle’s participation in Dutch markets and business models from first principles: diving deep into regulations, modelling revenue-per-asset, and trialling new propositions at pace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak Dutch and fluent English. Other European languages will also be an asset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will be doing</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning Axle’s commercial results in the Dutch market: pipeline, revenue and partner success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Winning new customers end-to-end, from first conversation through to commercial close, and setting partners up to generate meaningful revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving go-to-market execution with partners, including value propositions, pricing, customer segmentation and launch strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building the zero-to-one of the business through partnerships. You’ll be on the phone (and eventually on the ground) with utilities/retailers, potential clients and grid operators, creating and disproving hypotheses as quickly as possible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuing to sharpen our view of where the value is and which markets and business models are accessible to us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building lasting relationships with grid operators and the regulator, so that Axle is well positioned as the market evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as the conduit between partners and engineering, creating fast, structured feedback loops that turn field insights into product improvements</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As such, we are looking for a “full-stack operator” who can process highly technical information, ramp up commercial value, and accelerate us into new markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might have previous experience in one or more of the activities above, but we are more interested in your growth potential than your domain-specific expertise. We are looking for people who have built things, developed new relationships, and helped get big projects over the line in complex environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to deliver first-of-a-kind projects in one of Europe’s most important flexibility markets, become a domain expert, and work at the bleeding edge of electrification.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What’s in it for you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a 12 month fixed-term contract. Compensation is highly competitive and dependent on experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate with a deliberately flat structure and aim to keep pay equitable across the company, with a 1:1 median ratio between founder and team compensation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bi-annual retreats to strengthen team connection &amp; shared purpose.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be based in the Netherlands. To maximise collaboration, we ask that you spend ~1 week per month working from our London office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to directly shape the future of energy markets and accelerate the transition to a low-carbon world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are <em>extremely</em> keen to build a diverse team, and we’re particularly eager to hear from candidates who don't fit the traditional role stereotypes. If you’re motivated by our mission, please do reach out, even if you feel you might not ‘check all the boxes’.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Interview process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take-home exercise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final interview (in-person)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer, references, and welcome to the team!</p></li></ol><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/axle-careers/international-expansion-netherlands-268798","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1793990414},{"slug":"junior-or-medior-ai-engineer-rotterdam-368271","company_name":"Helloprint","title":"Junior or Medior AI Engineer","description":"<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><span style="color:#1a1a1a">HelloPrint is rebuilding the entire platform: new frontend, new pricing engine, new content engine, new product engine, everything ready for an agentic future. No one on the team writes code manually for what these systems handle. You'll work inside this rebuild, under the direction of our founding team (Hans, CEO, and Michael, CIO/Chief AI Officer), executing on high-leverage AI problems with real commercial impact, visible immediately in revenue or cost. There's no management layer between you and the outcome. You build, you ship, you measure, you move to the next problem.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">What you will build:</span></strong></h4><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><span style="color:#1A1A1A">The opportunity surface is large: 14 markets, 600,000 customers, a platform being rebuilt in parallel across four core engines. You'll work on problems from areas like:</span></p><ul class="[li_&]:mb-0 [li_&]:mt-1 [li_&]:gap-1 [&:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1"><li><p><span style="color:#1A1A1A">Dynamic pricing and margin optimization across markets.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1A1A1A">Agentic procurement: supplier selection, ordering, quality management.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1A1A1A">Customer journey automation from configuration to post-delivery.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1A1A1A">Intelligent content and SEO infrastructure at platform scale.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1A1A1A">Predictive demand and inventory across the supplier network.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1A1A1A">Internal tooling that multiplies the output of every team.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="color:#121317">Before you read further</span></h4><p><span style="color:#121317">HelloPri</span><span style="color:#1A1A1A">nt is on a mission to become the world's leading infrastructure for customizable printed products. From our offices in Rotterdam and Valencia, 100+ professionals from 20+ nationalities are building an AI-first company that scales output faster than headcount. We're at EUR 100M revenue and aiming to disrupt a trillion-dollar industry. Every hire we make needs to help get us there.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Commercial instinct first, engineering second.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You think about what something is worth before you think about how to build it.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Full-time in Rotterdam</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">. Five days a week, in the building where the transformation is happening. </span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">You have been building since before it was a career.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Side projects, tools, systems nobody asked for. The obsession came first.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#1A1A1A">You ship continuously.</span></strong><span style="color:#1A1A1A"> You ship fast and you ship real systems. Not prototypes, not demos.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">You are more than just an engineer.</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You understand product decisions, user impact, and design tradeoffs. You do not need a PM to translate the business problem for you.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><img style="width:1600px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/3vle3osbh4pt85p2evkmn5l1u1k64g/Michael_en_Hans.jpeg"></figure> <br> <h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Who you are:</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">You've built and shipped real production systems, not just contributed to someone else's. You're comfortable with ambiguity and don't need a fully specified brief to start. You care about what your work is worth, not just whether it works. You want to build inside a company that's already proven, not another 0-to-1 bet. You do not think of yourself as an AI engineer. You think of yourself as someone who solves hard problems and builds the systems to prove it. The engineering is the method. The obsession is the identity.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">Three signals that tell us you are that person:</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">You've spotted an opportunity for an AI solution before anyone assigned it to you, and built it, even if it started as a side project or a shortcut nobody asked for. Ask you to name one and it won't take you long.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">What you've shipped has been in production and actually used, not a prototype sitting in a repo or a demo that impressed someone once.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">You can point to at least one thing you built where you had a rough idea of what it was worth before building it, and checked afterward whether it delivered.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">Must-haves:</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">Hands-on production experience, not purely architectural or supervisory.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Commercial instinct that precedes technical execution: you know the business case before you write the first line.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">Track record of shipping production AI/software systems that are live and used by real users.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">Solid fluency in LLMs, agentic workflows, and modern AI infrastructure.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">Ability to reason about commercial impact, not just technical correctness.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">Comfortable working with high autonomy and limited process.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#1a1a1a">Office-first: on-site in Rotterdam, five days a week.</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><figure style="text-align:center;"><iframe height="538" width="957" src="//www.youtube.com/embed/CrRZjqfxJvs"></iframe></figure><p><br></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#121317">This role is not for you if you:</span></strong></h4><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><span style="color:#1A1A1A">This role is not for people who got into AI because it became important. It is for people who have been building since before anyone called it a career. The kind of person who coded as a teenager, shipped their first thing before anyone asked, and has never really stopped. Who finds it genuinely difficult to explain why they build: it is just what they do. Who would rather spend a Sunday solving a hard systems problem than almost anything else. If you have to think about whether that description fits you, it probably does not.<br></span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Got into AI because it became an important skill, not because you could not imagine doing anything else.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Need a brief, a PM, or a defined scope before taking action.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Measure your output in technical quality or feature count rather than business impact.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Would answer 'what would you build first?' with an infrastructure question.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">If you think a workweek of 40h is a lot.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Prefer hybrid or remote working.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><img style="width:4240px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/sdcwnus1nvv63dc17oatm92eoonwef/HelloPrint.jpg"></figure><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">What we offer</span></strong></h3><ul class="[li_&]:mb-0 [li_&]:mt-1 [li_&]:gap-1 [&:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">🎯 </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Room to grow: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">opportunities develop fast, within your role and across HelloPrint</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">🌍 </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">The team:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> 100+ people from 20+ nationalities who build at a pace most companies cannot match. Rotterdam is not a compromise. It is where the work happens.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">🚀 </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Real impact:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> shape the future of a high-growth, AI-driven company where your ideas land in production the same week.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">💡 </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Full autonomy from day one:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> no roadmap to follow, no brief to wait for. You see the problem, you build the solution, you own the outcome.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">🏃🏻‍♂️‍➡️ </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Hello-Benefits: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">including 24/7 HelloFit gym access, UrbanSportsClub discount, the best events and company-sponsored healthy meals every day</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">💶 Base salary:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> </span><span style="color:#1A1A1A">€50,000 to €75,000 gross per year, depending on skills, level and experience.</span></p></li></ul><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Ready to build something?</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> We need bold thinkers, fast executors, and AI-first problem solvers. If that sounds like you, apply now. Let's redefine an industry together.<br></span></p><p><em><span style="color:#121317">At HelloPrint, we believe diversity makes us better. We're building a workplace where everyone can be themselves, grow, and do their best work regardless of background, identity, or perspective. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/helloprint/junior-or-medior-ai-engineer-rotterdam-368271","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793989880},{"slug":"ai-engineer-l-young-talent-program-rotterdam-83216","company_name":"Helloprint","title":"AI Engineer l Young Talent Program","description":"<h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">The rules of building are being rewritten. Come write them with us.</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#121317">Every few decades, the way companies are built gets reinvented from scratch. That is happening right now, and the people who learn to build in this new world first will define the next twenty years. Superstars are being made this year, not in ten.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">HelloPrint is a €100M+ e-commerce company serving businesses across Europe and the US. We are rebuilding the entire company as AI-first: our platform, customer service, operations, and how we design, price, sell, and deliver. Every piece of technology we run is being rewritten as we speak.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317"><br>We are doing it with a small, senior, very fast AI development team working shoulder to shoulder with our business leads. </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">Now we are opening a handful of seats for young builders who want to grow faster than any graduate scheme, bootcamp, or big-tech ladder could ever let them.</span></strong></p><p><em><span style="color:#121317"><br></span></em><span style="color:#121317">We don't care if you are 16, 25 or 30, whether you are self-taught, hacking in high school, or finishing a degree at TU Delft or TU/e—we care about what you have built and how fast you solve hard problems. </span><em><span style="color:#121317"><br><br>The HelloPrint AI Residency is how you start. It is a permanent role from day one: your first year is a structured residency where you rotate across our most important AI projects, build alongside the team and learn at full speed. After that, you keep growing - in the direction where you have the most impact.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><img style="width:1600px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/3vle3osbh4pt85p2evkmn5l1u1k64g/Michael_en_Hans.jpeg"></figure><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">What you will actually do:</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#121317">You will not get a training plan, a sandbox project or six months of shadowing. From week one, you build real things that real customers and colleagues use, on the projects that matter most to the company. You sit next to the founders, next to the engineers who are rebuilding our platform, and next to the business leads who own the outcomes. You get a lot of freedom and real responsibility, plus honest, direct guidance and feedback from people who have built this before.<br></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">The kind of work you could be on in your first months:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Agentic Commerce</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: making HelloPrint discoverable and orderable through AI assistants, so a customer can order business cards from inside a chat.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">AI Design Studio</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: letting customers create a print-ready design from a single sentence.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">AI-first customer service</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: replacing classic ticketing with agents that resolve questions, check artwork and handle orders end to end.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Internal agent swarms</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: automating finance, purchasing, pricing and operations work that today still takes people hours.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Whatever you spot next</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: if you see something we should build, you pitch it, and if it is good, you build it.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><em><span style="color:#121317">We work with almost every modern framework and model, and we change our tools the moment something better appears. You will ship, measure, throw away and ship again - every week.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure style="text-align:center;"><iframe height="507" width="903" src="//www.youtube.com/embed/CrRZjqfxJvs"></iframe></figure> <br> <h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you are:</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">You are a builder before anything else</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">. You have shipped things nobody asked you to build: an app, an agent, a bot, a tool your friends actually use, a side business, an open-source contribution, a weird experiment that taught you something. You probably have more GitHub commits, demos or deployed projects than most people twice your age.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">You are extremely curious and extremely critical.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You read the new model release the day it drops and try it that evening. You question every assumption, including ours, and you can explain why. You are never satisfied with "it works" — you want to know why it works, and how it could be ten times better.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">You want to get better every single day, and you treat feedback as fuel rather than criticism.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You take ownership: when something breaks, you fix it; when something is unclear, you go and find out.</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">You have a solid grasp of backend and software fundamentals</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> (Python, APIs, databases) or the raw learning capacity to pick them up in weeks.<br></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">You will probably recognise yourself in most of this:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You build with AI every day: Claude, Cursor, Lovable, agents, APIs, whatever gets you there fastest.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You can show us concrete proof of work, not just tell us about it.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You move fast without being sloppy, and you care about the details the customer sees.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You are comfortable not knowing the answer, and you find it quickly.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You communicate clearly in English, in writing and out loud.<br></span></p></li></ul><p><em><span style="color:#000000"><br>What we do not require: a degree, a minimum age, years of experience or a perfect CV. If you are still in school or university, we will make it work around that.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><img style="width:4240px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/sdcwnus1nvv63dc17oatm92eoonwef/HelloPrint.jpg"></figure><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">What you get:</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#000000">The honest pitch: </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">you will learn more here in one year than in five years almost anywhere else</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">, because you will be building real systems for a real company that is reinventing itself, with the people who are leading that change.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000"><br>A contract from day one. The Residency is your first year at HelloPrint, not a trial period or an internship.</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Direct access to the founders</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> and to a senior AI development team who review your work and push you.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Ownership from day one</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: your name on projects that change how a €100M+ company runs.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">The best tools, no budget debates</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: the newest models, coding agents and frameworks, as soon as they are worth using.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">A growth path that follows your output, not your age</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: if you outgrow your role in six months, your role grows with you.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">A fast, flat, no-politics team</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> in Rotterdam, with a hands-on culture and a high bar.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Flexible set-up</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: full-time, or part-time alongside your studies. We care about what you deliver.<br></span></p></li></ul><p><em><span style="color:#000000">Salary and contract are tailored to your situation and your level, and we pay properly for real talent.<br></span></em></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">How to apply:</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#000000">Skip the cover letter. Show us what you have built.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Send us three things:</span></p><ol><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Your best project</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: a link to something you built: a live product, a repo, a demo video. Tell us in a few sentences what it does and what you would do differently now.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Something you think is broken</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: one thing about HelloPrint (our website, our ordering flow, anything) that you would rebuild with AI, and how you would do it.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">A short intro</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: who you are and what you are obsessed with right now. Five sentences is plenty.<br></span></p></li></ol><h3><span style="color:#000000">What happens next:</span></h3><ol><li><p><span style="color:#000000">We read every application ourselves and reply within 5 days if you’re up to the next round</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A 15-minute call with one of our builders or founders about your projects.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A Builders Day in our office: Together with other builders, you meet the team and if we have a click, you work on an assignment</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A conversation with the founders, and a decision the same day.<br></span></p></li></ol><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em><span style="color:#121317">We would rather hear from you too early than too late. If you are not sure you are ready, apply anyway;&nbsp; your work will answer that question for us. At HelloPrint, we believe diversity makes us better. We're building a workplace where everyone can be themselves, grow, and do their best work regardless of background, identity, or perspective. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/helloprint/ai-engineer-l-young-talent-program-rotterdam-83216","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793989880},{"slug":"it-internship-fullstack-engineer-cloud-native-platform-engineering-developer-experience-rotterdam-477686","company_name":"Swisscom","title":"IT Internship - Fullstack Engineer: Cloud-Native Platform Engineering & Developer Experience","description":"<p><strong><em><span style="font-size:1.1em">IT Internship - Cloud-Native Platform Engineering &amp; Developer Experience (AnyOrg)</span></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><span style="font-size:1.1em">Becoming an IT professional that you aspire to be</span></em></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>About the Internship</strong></p><p class="ParagraphBase-sc-1npqnwg-9 Paragraph-sc-1npqnwg-10 hoDOtt slate-p">Swisscom is always keen on attracting and developing the best talents. As part of the leading telecom and tech company in Switzerland, you will work on real projects that have real impact. From day one, you will be part of an international team collaborating across Switzerland, Rotterdam, and Riga, contributing to innovative solutions in Swisscom’s digital transformation. This means working hands‑on in backend, cloud, or full‑stack development, applying your Computer Science skills to real technical challenges.</p><p class="ParagraphBase-sc-1npqnwg-9 Paragraph-sc-1npqnwg-10 hoDOtt slate-p">With colleagues from over 60 nationalities, diversity is not just something we value, it is how we work. We believe in open collaboration, ownership, and continuous learning. You will be encouraged to share ideas, take initiative, and grow within the environment. We respect each other, help each other out, and are not afraid to make mistakes. We make sure you can be the best version of yourself.</p><p class="ParagraphBase-sc-1npqnwg-9 Paragraph-sc-1npqnwg-10 hoDOtt slate-p">Our internship program starts<strong> </strong>on <strong>1st</strong> <strong>February 2027</strong>. In this <strong>6 months internship</strong> you will work in agile teams using Scrum and SAFe, gaining hands-on experience in a fast-paced and supportive environment.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>About the Internship Project: </strong></p><p><strong>Cloud-Native Platform Engineering &amp; Developer Experience (AnyOrg)</strong></p><p>Join a team building enterprise platform services used by engineers across Swisscom. You will work on cloud-native Front/backed services, platform automation, CI/CD pipelines, developer tooling and security integrations. The project offers hands-on experience with modern software engineering practices, DevOps, GitLab pipelines and cloud technologies while collaborating with experienced engineers in an international Agile environment.</p> <br> <p><strong>Must-haves: </strong>TypeScript; Git  <br><strong>Nice-to-haves: </strong>Angular; AWS; Docker; Kubernetes; UX/UI; CSS</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Who are you?</strong></p><ul><li><p>You are a student enrolled in the <strong>last year</strong> of your HBO or University program in the field of Computer Science, Informatica, or any other similar field.</p></li><li><p>You <strong>live in the</strong> <strong>Netherlands.</strong></p></li><li><p>You are willing to contribute to an international team and you have an agile mindset.</p></li><li><p>You are curious and responsible.</p></li><li><p>You have a good level of English; any other language is a plus.</p><p><br><strong>Please note that for non-EU students, it is necessary to provide the NUFFIC Agreement for the 6-month internship from your university in order to be eligible.</strong><br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Perks</strong></p><ul><li><p>810 € gross Monthly Allowance (Full time)</p></li><li><p>IT Equipment</p></li><li><p>Agile working environment and lean management instructor</p></li><li><p>Flexible working time model</p></li><li><p>Plenty of opportunities for training and personal development</p></li><li><p>International Environment</p></li><li><p>Holidays &amp; time off</p></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Contact</strong></p><p>Do you have any questions or do you want to know why we love working at Swisscom? Feel free to reach out to Lilla Egyed (<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- or María Baker (<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- </p><p> </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Please, submit your CV in English.</strong></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/swisscom/it-internship-fullstack-engineer-cloud-native-platform-engineering-developer-experience-rotterdam-477686","tags":["IT & DevOps"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793989879},{"slug":"account-executive-dach-amsterdam-123797","company_name":"Tellent","title":"Account Executive  - DACH","description":"<h4>About the Role</h4><p>We're building the sales engine for Tellent HR in the DACH market, and we're looking for an Account Executive to help us do it. Think of it as joining a startup inside a scale-up.</p><p>First and foremost, this is a hands-on selling role. You'll own the full sales cycle for Tellent HR (Manage and/or Grow), split roughly 80/20 between new business and expansion into our existing customer base. Inbound isn't going to be your main pipeline driver, so expect to spend around 50% of your time prospecting, against ambitious daily and weekly activity targets. Alongside that, you'll help us work out <em>how</em> we win in DACH: testing motions fast and doubling down on what drives revenue.</p><p>You'll work with a dedicated Product Marketing Manager and Customer Success Manager in the Tellent HR squad. CS capacity is limited, though, so you'll run deals independently, including demos and follow-through.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Your 12-Month Journey</h4><ul><li><p><strong>First 3 months:</strong> Learn Tellent HR, our ideal customers and the competitive landscape in DACH. Build your first pipeline through outbound, establish a consistent daily activity rhythm, and close your first deals.</p></li><li><p><strong>Within 6 months:</strong> Consistently hit your activity, pipeline and revenue targets, understand which sales motions work best in the DACH market, and feed insights back to Product Marketing and Product.</p></li><li><p><strong>After 1 year:</strong> Be the go-to expert on selling Tellent HR in DACH, with a repeatable, data-backed playbook that others can pick up.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What You'll Be Doing</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Own the full sales cycle, independently:</strong> Run 1–3 month, multi-stakeholder deals involving HR leaders, founders/CEOs and Finance, from first touch through to close and follow-through.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hunt for new pipeline (around 50% of your time):</strong> Prospect by phone, email and LinkedIn, consistently hit your daily and weekly activity targets, and maintain 3–4x pipeline coverage. Partner, CS and marketing leads are a bonus, not the plan.</p></li><li><p><strong>Drive expansion:</strong> Prospect into existing Tellent customers to cross-sell and upsell, e.g. Recruitee customers adding Tellent HR, or Manage customers adding Grow.</p></li><li><p><strong>Sell on value:</strong> Run consultative discovery and tailored demos, position on business outcomes, and handle objections, including against key competitors (with support from PMM).</p></li><li><p><strong>Manage deals with discipline:</strong> Use mutual action plans, keep HubSpot accurate (including SPICED), forecast reliably and disqualify early.</p></li><li><p><strong>Test and build, alongside selling:</strong> Experiment with sales motions, sequences and verticals, help build the playbook with our PMM, and bring customer and competitive insights from the DACH market back to Product and Marketing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What You Bring</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Early-stage DNA:</strong> You've sold in a startup or early scale-up and built pipeline and processes where none existed. You know what it means to be an early sales hire.</p></li><li><p><strong>Proven hunter:</strong> A track record of self-generating pipeline through outbound and consistently hitting ambitious activity targets. You genuinely enjoy picking up the phone and creating opportunities from scratch.</p></li><li><p><strong>B2B SaaS sales experience:</strong> You've closed new business (ideally expansion too) as a fully autonomous AE in a startup or early scale-up, running 1–5 month, multi-stakeholder sales cycles. HR tech experience is a plus, not essential.</p></li><li><p><strong>Self-sufficient and resilient:</strong> You don't wait for leads, support teams or perfect processes. You bounce back from rejection and stay disciplined through the ups and downs of building something new.</p></li><li><p><strong>Consultative and data-driven:</strong> Strong discovery, demo and negotiation skills. You anchor on value before price and know your numbers (pipeline, conversion, win rate and cycle time).</p></li><li><p><strong>Languages:</strong> Fluent English and native or fluent German are required. You'll be responsible for engaging customers and building relationships across the DACH market.</p></li></ul><p>This role probably isn't for you if you want a structured environment with large support teams and steady inbound, or you're more excited by GTM strategy than by picking up the phone every day.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>How We Measure Success</h4><ul><li><p>Closed-won revenue against target (primary KPI)</p></li><li><p>Daily and weekly outbound activity targets (key leading indicator, especially early on)</p></li><li><p>Self-generated pipeline and coverage</p></li><li><p>Win rate, deal velocity and forecast accuracy</p></li><li><p>Contributions to the playbook</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What We Offer</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Compensation:</strong> €55000–€70000 gross annual base salary, <strong>plus commission</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ownership and impact:</strong> Real autonomy to shape the sales motion, playbook and market strategy for a growing product line.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hybrid working:</strong> Work from our canal-side Amsterdam office 2–3 days per week.</p></li><li><p><strong>International environment:</strong> Join a diverse and international team working across multiple markets.</p></li><li><p><strong>Learning &amp; Development:</strong> €1,500 annual learning budget and 2 dedicated learning days.</p></li><li><p><strong>Pension &amp; Wellness:</strong> Pension plan and wellness perks.</p></li><li><p><strong>Time Off:</strong> 28 paid holiday days, plus 2 additional days in 2026.</p></li><li><p><strong>Work from Anywhere:</strong> Work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year.</p></li><li><p><strong>Commuting:</strong> Commuting and travel reimbursement.</p></li><li><p><strong>Home Office:</strong> €200 home office budget and a work-from-home allowance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Equipment:</strong> Apple MacBook and all the tools you need to succeed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>About Tellent</h4><p>Tellent is a leading Talent Management Suite designed to empower HR &amp; People teams across the entire employee journey. Our all-in-one platform combines an Applicant Tracking System (<strong>Tellent Recruitee</strong>), an intuitive HRIS (<strong>Tellent HR</strong>), and powerful Performance Management software (<strong>Tellent Grow</strong>).</p><p>With 250+ team members globally, 7,000+ customers in 100+ countries, and a growing ecosystem of 500+ partners, we help organizations attract, grow, and retain top talent — and we're just getting started.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>AI in Our Recruitment Process</h4><p>We use our internally developed AI tools to help streamline our recruitment process. However, technology never makes a decision. Every candidate is personally reviewed by our team. Your journey with us is guided by people, supported by tech. Curious about how it works? Read our <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://recruitee.com/ai-statement">AI Statement</a>, check our <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://recruitee.com/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, or chat with us at <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>If you require accommodations or support during the recruitment process, please let us know — we're happy to help.</em></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tellent/account-executive-dach-amsterdam-123797","tags":["1. GTM"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793989879},{"slug":"account-executive-benelux-amsterdam-106821","company_name":"Tellent","title":"Account E