sis/power-of-the-home"><strong><u>here</u></strong></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’re looking for a commercially sharp, highly autonomous operator to drive Axle’s commercial success in the German market.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Axle has quickly become the leader in our operational markets, and we’re now looking to expand our reach internationally. Our goal is to become the go-to platform for energy flexibility globally, and we’re hiring the person to make that happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will assess Axle’s participation in German markets and business models from first principles: diving deep into regulations, modelling revenue-per-asset, and trialling new propositions at pace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak German and fluent English. Other European languages are also an asset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will be doing</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning Axle’s commercial results in the German market: pipeline, revenue and partner success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Winning new customers end-to-end, from first conversation through to commercial close, and setting partners up to generate meaningful revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving go-to-market execution with partners, including value propositions, pricing, customer segmentation and launch strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building the zero-to-one of the business through partnerships. You’ll be on the phone (and on the ground) with utilities/retailers, potential clients and grid operators, creating and disproving hypotheses as quickly as possible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuing to sharpen our view of where the value is and which markets and business models are accessible to us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building lasting relationships with grid operators and the regulator, so that Axle is well positioned as the market evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as the conduit between partners and engineering, creating fast, structured feedback loops that turn field insights into product improvements</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As such, we are looking for a “full-stack operator” who can process highly technical information, ramp up commercial value, and accelerate us into new markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might have previous experience in one or more of the activities above, but we are more interested in your growth potential than your domain-specific expertise. We are looking for people who have built things, developed new relationships, and helped get big projects over the line in complex environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to repeatedly deliver first-of-a-kind projects across the world, become a domain expert, and work at the bleeding edge of global electrification.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What’s in it for you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a 12 month fixed-term contract. Compensation is highly competitive and dependent on experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate with a deliberately flat structure and aim to keep pay equitable across the company, with a 1:1 median ratio between founder and team compensation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bi-annual retreats to strengthen team connection &amp; shared purpose.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be based in the Germany. To maximise collaboration, we ask that you spend ~1 week per month working from our London office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to directly shape the future of energy markets and accelerate the transition to a low-carbon world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are <em>extremely</em> keen to build a diverse team, and we’re particularly eager to hear from candidates who don't fit the traditional role stereotypes. If you’re motivated by our mission, please do reach out, even if you feel you might not ‘check all the boxes’.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Interview process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take-home exercise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final interview (in-person)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer, references, and welcome to the team!</p></li></ol><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/axle-careers/international-expansion-germany-354371","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1793990414},{"slug":"strategy-operations-analyst-germany-berlin-157340","company_name":"Pennylane De","title":"Strategy & Operations Analyst - Germany 🇩🇪","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you looking to have an impact on the daily life of millions of entrepreneurs in France and Europe?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do you thrive in a trustful, fast-paced environment?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Then Pennylane might be the right place for you — and you, might be the perfect fit for this role 🙂</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our vision</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim to become the most beloved financial Operating System of European SMEs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We help business owners get rid of the time consuming hassle of handling accounting and finance, while giving them access to key information that they can use to make better decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meanwhile, we’re helping accountants. By using Pennylane, rather than doing manual and repetitive tasks, they can spend more time advising and guiding their clients.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pennylane is one of the fastest growing Fintechs in France (and we're accelerating in Germany 🇩🇪)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In 6 years of existence, we’ve managed to :</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 Make ourselves known as a groundbreaking accounting and financial software for small businesses and their accountants</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Raise a total of €400 millions, including from Sequoia, the famous fund from the Silicon Valley who invested early in companies like Google, Facebook, Airbnb, Stripe, Paypal and much more...</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 Grow from 7 cofounders to 1200+ happy Pennylaners : we’re now recognized as one of the greatest places to work in France (and also remotely), with a 4.6/5 rating on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="postings-link" href="https://www.glassdoor.fr/Avis/Pennylane-France-Avis-E4171708.htm">Glassdoor</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 Build an international environment with more than 25 nationalities, with a strong remote-friendly culture, where 30% of the employees are already working from all parts of Europe</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 Earn the trust of thousands of customers and accounting firms and obtain <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="postings-link" href="https://www.google.com/search?q=pennylane&amp;ei=O9pOYvm0Co-blwSmhKmIAw&amp;ved=0ahUKEwi5vsWL-4H3AhWPzYUKHSZCCjEQ4dUDCA4&amp;uact=5&amp;oq=pennylane&amp;gs_lcp=Cgdnd3Mtd2l6EAMyDQgAEIAEELEDEIMBEAoyCwguEIAEEMcBEK8BMgcIABCABBAKMgcIABCABBAKMgUIABCABDIFCAAQgAQyBQgAEIAEMgcIABCABBAKMgcIABCABBAKMgcIABCABBAKOgcIABBHELADOgkIABCwAxAKEEM6CgguEMcBEK8BEAo6BggAEBYQHjoICAAQFhAKEB46DQguEIAEEMcBEK8BEApKBAhBGABKBAhGGABQ7QFY6wVgugdoAXABeACAAUiIAbMCkgEBNZgBAKABAcgBCcABAQ&amp;sclient=gws-wiz">outstanding ratings</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Already more than 1 300,000 small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and over 6,500 accounting firms use Pennylane in France!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Strategy &amp; Operations at Pennylane:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Pennylane, being part of the Strategy &amp; Operations team means deeply understanding operational realities. As we launch our German entity, we design and implement efficient, scalable solutions that enable Pennylane to reach and exceed its ambitious expansion targets. Your role will be pivotal in structuring local operations from scratch, scaling existing processes, and tailoring our operating model to the specificities of the German market. To make this launch a success, our Strategy &amp; Operations teams work daily alongside Business teams (Sales, Success Managers), Tech teams (Developers, Product Managers), and Data teams (Data Scientists, Data Analysts).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Goal</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significantly boost team productivity through better tool utilization, process simplification, and operational structuring to support the launch and expansion of our German entity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Day-to-Day Impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the owner, key point of contact, and driver of change within the Business Teams for the German market. You will work closely with operational managers leading Sales, Professional Services, Customer Support, and Account Management.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive transformation and challenge the status quo:</strong> Observe, listen, challenge existing setups, and continuously propose optimizations to reduce time spent on manual admin tasks or data searches. You will pave the way for future local growth, structure operations for a new entity, and document all procedural changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Implement operational improvements:</strong> Roll out solution-driven initiatives through new information systems, app modifications, or organizational changes. You will lead projects while leveraging cross-functional capabilities (Data, Sales, Finance, etc.). Your mission will also be to ensure high customer satisfaction, hit delivery deadlines, and monitor roll-out KPIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale and localize processes:</strong> Adapt global operational frameworks to German market specificities while remaining aligned with core Pennylane standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benchmark and innovate:</strong> Observe other departments, take a step back, run benchmarks, and gather insights to refine operational strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enable teams and drive adoption:</strong> Implement strong communication and hands-on support for German teams to ensure smooth onboarding onto new methodologies (optimal tooling, training, continuous improvement). You will ensure daily tool adoption and process adherence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridge Ops and Corporate strategy:</strong> Gain a high-level view of corporate challenges to anticipate their impact on local German operations and provide operational visibility through data-driven insights.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Candidate Profile</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an ambitious professional with a proven track record in organizational transformation, productivity improvement, project management, and operational structuring in a fast-paced environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Qualifications &amp; Skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Languages: Fluent in German and English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum of 4 years of proven experience in business 