&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #236fa1;&quot;&gt;Our Commitment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verifone is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. Verifone is also committed to compliance with all fair employment practices regarding citizenship and immigration status.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/verifone/senior-paralegal-london-251293","tags":["Legal/BusDev"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1794023717},{"slug":"senior-devops-engineer-london-456296","company_name":"84674Th44Metrea9999","title":"Senior DevOps Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;isPasted&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metrea delivers effects-as-a-service to national security partners across five domains and more than a dozen mission areas. These include airborne ISR, electronic warfare, secure communications, aerial refueling, special air missions, aerial firefighting, and advanced simulation. We own the whole stack: designing, building, and operating turnkey capabilities that give our partners decisive, asymmetric advantage against rapidly evolving threats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our operating model is built around three interlocking pillars. The Support Groups provide a global shared-service – spanning people, finance, platform, operations, legal, and engagement. This frees up our Core Groups, who develop and own mission capabilities end-to-end, to focus entirely on delivery. The Market Groups apply a regional lens, ensuring that our agile and adaptable capabilities remain aligned to the wicked problems that matter most to our partners across the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of our model is a simple but powerful idea: be a true partner with skin in the game. Our partners need effects, not just equipment. By owning the full stack – from the lab to the field – we are able to drive a continuous cycle of innovation that keeps our partners ahead. It&#39;s a fast-moving, intellectually demanding environment where talented people are given real responsibility, work on problems that matter, and contribute to an enterprise that is growing quickly and deliberately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Washington, DC, with facilities across the United States, the United Kingdom, as well as Continental Europe and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Group Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within Platform Group area of Metrea. The Platform Group&amp;nbsp;rovides the Information Technology and Information Systems ecosystem that Metrea is utilising for the day-to-day operations, communication, collaboration and information sharing across its Platform business block.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead the design and operation of secure, reliable Azure platforms that enable Metrea&#39;s UK teams to build, deploy, and support mission-focused services with confidence. You will shape how we use Azure, Azure DevOps, GitHub, automation, and DevSecOps practices to improve delivery speed, platform resilience, and developer experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be successful if you can combine hands-on engineering depth with technical leadership: solving complex platform challenges, mentoring others, and making pragmatic decisions for sensitive defence environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and operate secure, scalable Azure platform services, primarily supporting MITO programmes and UK engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect Azure infrastructure through code, covering networking, identity, compute, storage, monitoring, governance and container platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve Azure DevOps and GitHub CI/CD pipelines for repeatable, controlled and secure software delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop secure deployment patterns for AI-assisted and agentic workflows, including model integrations, automated evaluation and controlled releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy and secure AI platform components such as model APIs, LLM workloads and MCP servers, with appropriate access controls, secrets management and data boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimise containerised workloads using Docker and AKS, with resilient and repeatable deployment patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement DevSecOps practices including policy as code, vulnerability management, secrets management and software supply-chain controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish effective monitoring, logging, alerting and service-health reporting across platforms and workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex infrastructure, networking, identity, security, pipeline and production issues affecting business-critical services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise and mentor engineers, promote effective platform practices and help teams adopt reusable, self-service tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a senior DevOps, platform, cloud or infrastructure engineering role supporting business-critical services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience designing, deploying and operating Microsoft Azure environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with Azure DevOps or GitHub, including CI/CD pipelines, release controls and deployment automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven infrastructure-as-code experience using Terraform, Bicep, ARM templates or comparable technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Docker, Kubernetes and AKS, including resilient and automated deployment patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing DevSecOps controls across infrastructure, pipelines and the software supply chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building AI-assisted or agentic development workflows, with exposure to model APIs, LLM deployments or MCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting capability across cloud infrastructure, networking, identity, observability and software delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence technical direction, mentor engineers and work effectively across software, platform, security and support teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploying or operating locally hosted LLMs or GPU-based model-serving infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Securing MCP servers, agent permissions and access to sensitive tools or data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backstage or another internal developer platform, including reusable templates and self-service workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in defence, government or another regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
