m, and where your work genuinely helps people live longer, healthier lives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Role Purpose</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Field Service Engineer supporting our London clinics, you will play a critical role in ensuring the performance, availability, and continuous improvement of Neko Health’s clinical scanning technology across both existing and upcoming UK sites. You will lead installation, maintenance, servicing, upgrades, and retrofits of instruments to guarantee consistently high uptime for clinical teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partnering closely with Engineering, Clinical Operations, and cross‑functional teams across the UK and Europe, you will serve as the vital link between real‑world field performance and product development capturing insights that drive improvements in technology, processes, service quality, and member experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role blends hands‑on technical expertise with collaboration, problem‑solving, and operational ownership to ensure seamless clinic operations as we continue scaling in the UK.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Deliver in the First 6–12 Months</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Successfully install, maintain, and service scanning instruments across London clinics, ensuring high reliability and minimal downtime.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong working relationships with Engineering and Clinical Operations, turning field insights into actionable product and process improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish consistent documentation, reporting, and compliance standards across all UK installation and service activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to enhance service efficiency, instrument performance, and preventative maintenance strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the sca