nalyst Apprentice to join our fast-paced EU Finance department. Reporting directly to the Regional Finance Director, you will work alongside experienced professionals, gain hands-on experience, and join a global community with technical training, mentorship, and regular networking opportunities to accelerate your growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Through a structured three-year program, you will balance real team deliverables with study towards your ACCA (Association of Chartered Certified Accountants) qualification, dedicating 20% of your time (around six hours per week) to your professional studies. Each placement will be supported by a dedicated Rotation Manager alongside guidance from senior Finance leadership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will gain broad exposure across six core finance pillars: Financial Control and Revenue &amp; Billing in year one; Tax and Treasury in year two; and Strategic Finance and Finance Transformation in year three. Depending on business and ACCA requirements, you may also gain exposure to adjacent areas such as Product Control, Procurement, or Internal Audit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How You’ll Make An Impact</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support accurate, timely finance operations across your rotations, contributing to processes such as month-end close, reconciliations, journals and variance analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help teams deliver invoicing, settlement, revenue recognition, tax compliance, cash management, budgeting and reporting activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and review information carefully, including supporting audit, compliance and management reporting requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with colleagues across Finance to respond to queries, share information and deliver tasks to agreed deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Look for practical ways to improve processes, documentation and the use of finance systems and data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply what you learn through ACCA study to real finance work, building technical, analytical and communication skills over time.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Eligibility Requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is offered as a government-funded Level 7 ACCA apprenticeship. Appointment is conditional on the successful candidate meeting the government’s apprenticeship funding and eligibility requirements at the start of training, as confirmed by our approved training provider. Under current England funding rules, Level 7 funding is generally available to applicants aged 16–21, with limited exceptions for eligible applicants aged 22–24 who have an EHCP or have been, or are, in care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is offered as an early-careers opportunity and we are not able to offer this role on a privately funded basis. Further information about the Apprenticeship funding can be found here.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Academic Qualifications: </strong>You will have either:</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree qualification</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">OR</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have completed a Level 4 AAT qualification before the September start date</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">+ 2 A Levels (or equivalent) and 3 GCSEs including a pass in English and Maths </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visa sponsorship: </strong>We are unable to offer visa sponsorship for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Academic Ambition: You are eager to begin your journey toward becoming a Chartered Accountant via the ACCA pathway.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical Mindset: You have a natural comfort with numbers and a high attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resilience: The ability to work toward tight deadlines in a fast-paced, high-growth work environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tech Savvy: Proficiency in Excel or Google Sheets. Any prior exposure to accounting systems (like Workday) is a huge plus, but not a dealbreaker—we will train you!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communication: Excellent verbal and written communication skills and a "team player" attitude.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with Excel or Google Sheets; familiarity with finance systems such as Workday is helpful, but not essential.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/2027-finance-degree-apprenticeship-london-339099","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794022824},{"slug":"engineer-i-it-engineering-london-313818","company_name":"Checkout.com","title":"Engineer I,  IT Engineering","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Company Description</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://checkout.com"><em> </em></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><em>Checkout.com</em></a><em>. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. </em><br /><br /><em>Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. </em><br /><br /><em>If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. </em><br /><br /><em>With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced IT Engineer II to join Checkout’s IT Engineering team, supporting Workplace Technology. In this generalist role, you will work across the services and platforms managed by the team, helping colleagues get the technology they need while keeping those services secure, reliable, and easy to use.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will contribute across areas such as identity and access, end-user devices, collaboration and productivity platforms, IT assets and licences, and office technology. You are not expected to be a subject matter expert in every product. Instead, you bring strong technical foundations, depth in one or more areas, and the curiosity to build working knowledge across the wider portfolio.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At this level, you can confidently resolve all but the most complex problems affecting the team. You will own operational outcomes, deliver small-to-medium projects independently, and work with colleagues and stakeholders to improve the services we provide across Checkout.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How You’ll Make an Impact</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Portfolio Service Ownership:</strong> Administer and improve services across the Workplace Technology portfolio. This may include Okta, Google Workspace, Atlassian, macOS and Windows endpoint management through tools such as Jamf and Microsoft Intune, IT asset and licence processes, and office technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Identity and Access:</strong> Support secure identity lifecycle and access management, including joiner, mover, and leaver activities, single sign-on, group and role administration, and least-privilege access.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-User Technology:</strong> Help manage and support company endpoints and workplace services. Apply approved configurations and security controls, troubleshoot issues, and contribute to a consistent employee experience across platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform Administration:</strong> Configure and maintain team-managed applications and services. Learn unfamiliar platforms quickly, follow established governance, and identify when a change needs specialist or security review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational Excellence:</strong> Provide dependable operational support, maintain clear documentation and runbooks, and help the team improve service quality, reliability, and supportability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>I</strong>ncident and Change Management: Own incidents through the full lifecycle, from triage, prioritisation, and stakeholder communication through safe service restoration, root-cause analysis, and follow-up actions. Maintain accurate incident records, capture decisions and remediation, and document recurring issues and operational procedures in clear, current runbooks and knowledge articles. Plan and implement changes safely, with appropriate testing, approvals, and rollback plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project Delivery:</strong> Plan and deliver small-to-medium technical projects, coordinating with stakeholders and other teams to manage dependencies, risks, and outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automation and Improvement:</strong> Identify repeatable manual work and service friction. Propose or build appropriately controlled automation and simpler workflows to reduce toil and improve consistency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Asset and Licence Management:</strong> Support accurate technology inventory, licence administration, and lifecycle processes, helping the team make effective and responsible use of its tools and equipment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Knowledge Sharing:</strong> Share learning across the team, contribute to onboarding and operational guidance, and support colleagues as they develop their technical skills.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>What We’re Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> Typically 2-3+ years in IT engineering, workplace technology, systems administration, or a similar technical role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Breadth:</strong> Practical experience supporting or administering a range of workplace technology services. You have a strong foundation in at least one relevant area and are motivated to build capability across others.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relevant Platforms:</strong> Experience with some of the following is useful: identity and access management (for example, Okta and SSO); Google Workspace; Atlassian products; macOS or Windows endpoint management (for example, Jamf or Microsoft Intune); SaaS administration; IT asset or licence management; or office technology. You do not need experience with every product listed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Security Mindset:</strong> Understand the importance of least privilege, secure configuration, data protection, auditability, and careful change management. You know when to escalate a risk or seek specialist guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Problem Solving:</strong> Take a logical, evidence-led approach to troubleshooting. Explain technical options and trade-offs clearly, and distinguish between immediate mitigation and long-term resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership:</strong> Take responsibility for work from investigation through resolution and follow-up. Care about the long-term health of the services you support, not only closing individual requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication:</strong> Work effectively with colleagues, stakeholders, and technical teams. Translate technical detail into clear updates and provide helpful, user-focused support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adaptability:</strong> Comfortable working across a varied technology estate, learning new tools, and balancing planned delivery with operational priorities in a changing environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Teamwork:</strong> Share knowledge, ask for help when needed, and contribute positively to a team that works across multiple technical domains.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Information</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring all of you to work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life at </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com"><strong>Checkout.com</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.checkout.com/careers"> <u>Careers Page</u></a> to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a closer look at daily life at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Checkout.com">Checkout.com</a>, follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/checkout/life/"><u>LinkedIn</u></a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/checkout_com/"><u>Instagram</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkoutcom/engineer-i-it-engineering-london-313818","tags":["All Departments"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1794022824},{"slug":"scientific-software-engineer-lab-integration-london-33388","company_name":"Cuspai","title":"Scientific Software Engineer (Lab Integration)","description":"<h2>About CuspAI </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CuspAI is the frontier AI company on a mission to solve the breakthrough materials needed to power human progress. While nature took billions of years to perfect molecules, we are harnessing AI to unlock trillion-dollar materials breakthroughs in months, not millennia. Our founding team is the most cited in the world, comprised of world-class researchers in AI, chemistry and engineering.<br /><br />We are working on some of the hardest and most important challenges including energy, clean water, the future of compute, and carbon capture, and this is just the start of what our 'search engine' for next-generation materials will unlock.<br /><br />We invite you to be part of a diverse, innovative team at the intersection of AI and materials science, working to create impactful partnerships that drive innovation, scalability, and industry collaboration. This work matters. Your work matters.<br /><br /><strong>We’re on the cusp of the on-demand materials era. Join us.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are seeking a Scientific Software Engineer to build and run the systems that connect our AI platform to physical laboratories around the world. Together with the team, you will shape the software layer of our closed-loop discovery workflow: our agents propose experiments, partner labs execute them, and the results feed back into our models to guide the next set of experiments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role sits between lab automation and production engineering. You will bring hands-on experience with scientific or lab automation, and the engineering discipline to make those integrations secure, reliable and scalable across many partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be part of a small team of materials scientists, ML engineers and software engineers, working closely with each other and with our partner labs. You will help define how our AI platform connects to the physical world and shape the tools and practices that link external partner labs to our platform. You will thrive here if you enjoy collaborating across disciplines and learning from people whose expertise differs from your own.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Impact</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will turn experimental labs into first-class, programmable parts of the CuspAI platform. Every partner you onboard, and every integration you harden, shortens the loop between an AI-generated hypothesis and a validated material.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape how we connect to partner labs around the world, accounting for different levels of automation and AI-readiness, then design, build and operate the services that send experiment requests from our AI agents and reliably bring results back.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build APIs and data models (e.g. FastAPI, Pydantic) for bidirectional lab-to-cloud data exchange.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate with lab instruments, robotic platforms, LIMS/ELN systems and scheduling software, translating between disparate formats and CuspAI's data platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make integrations reliable at scale: idempotency, retries, queueing, monitoring and alerting across many partners and time zones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with the technical onboarding of new lab partners, assessing their systems and setting up integrations quickly and repeatedly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate day to day with experimental materials scientists, optimisation experts and engineers on the team, co-designing workflows and feeding lab realities back into platform design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deploy and run containerised services on cloud infrastructure, with testing and CI/CD as standard.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Must Have Skills and Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with lab automation, self-driving labs or other scientific discovery workflows, e.g. instrument control, robotic platforms, or high-throughput experimentation data pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong software engineering background, with production experience building and operating backend services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep fluency in Python, including typed, well-tested code and API design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing distributed systems that integrate with external parties: APIs, message queues or event-driven architectures, and data contracts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of security practices for externally facing systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative mindset: you enjoy working in a small, multidisciplinary team, and can communicate clearly with experimental scientists, optimisation experts and engineers alike.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Points</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experimental lab experience in materials science, chemistry or chemical engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with workflow orchestration (e.g. Dagster, Flyte, Prefect) or active learning loops.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with infrastructure as code (e.g. Terraform) and observability tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Security or compliance experience or handling partner IP and confidential data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working across distributed teams and multiple time zones.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A competitive salary:</strong> We value and reward impact and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity in CuspAI:</strong> You have a stake in the success of the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off to stay fresh:</strong> 28 days holiday (DE, NL, UK) or 21 days holiday (JP, SG, US), in addition to local public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>‘Gold Standard’ parental leave:</strong> 26 weeks (primary caregiver) and 12 weeks (secondary caregiver) at full pay - we look after you and your family while we work on the most important materials discovery problems together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional development budget:</strong> We invest in your career development so you can stay up to date with the latest industry knowledge or add to your skills to increase impact and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solve meaningful problems:</strong> See how your work has a direct impact on advancing materials science and solving sustainability and climate-related problems through the creation and application of bleeding-edge SOTA technology and revolutionary techniques</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True interdisciplinary teamwork:</strong> Be part of a deeply collaborative environment bridging AI research, computational chemistry, and experimental science - work with world-class researchers and engineers who enjoy sharing knowledge and supporting each other</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Join us in shaping the future of materials with AI. Together, we can create groundbreaking solutions for a more sustainable world.</strong><br /><br /><br /><strong>CuspAI is an equal opportunities employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace</strong>. We do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citi