elop effective threat models and mitigation strategies.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Strategic Planning: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Translate business objectives into technical strategy and ensure technical roadmaps align with long-term client goals.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Agile Practices: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Expertise in Agile methodologies, with a focus on resolving impediments and driving adoption across teams.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Client Engagement: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Communicate effectively with clients, manage expectations, and provide practical, risk-based security recommendations.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Continuous Improvement &amp; Collaboration: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Drive innovation, adopt emerging security practices, share knowledge, and support team success.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#121317">What you'll bring:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">We are seeking a highly technical expert with a strong focus on mobile platform security. You should bring:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mobile Security Expertise: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Strong hands-on knowledge of Android and iOS security fundamentals, common mobile threats and vulnerabilities, security architecture, controls, and mitigation techniques.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mobile Security Testing: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Practical experience in mobile penetration testing, security assessments, threat modelling, and implementing or assessing security controls.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Security Problem Solving: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">A systematic and analytical approach to identifying, investigating, and resolving mobile security issues.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Authentication &amp; Cryptography: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Strong understanding of authentication, authorisation, cryptography, encryption, and secure design principles, with the ability to recommend appropriate cryptographic controls.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Continuous Improvement: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">A proactive approach to improving security practices, tooling, controls, and ways of working.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Desirable knowledge &amp; experience:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mobile Security Tooling &amp; Analysis: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Experience with reverse engineering, analysis techniques, and tools such as Burp Suite Pro, Frida, Objection, JADX, IDA Pro, Hopper, Radare, ADB, Apktool, YARA, Xcode, and Android Studio.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Mobile Development &amp; DevSecOps: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Knowledge of Android/iOS development, secure development practices, DevSecOps tooling, testing, and automation frameworks.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Development &amp; Reverse Engineering: </span></strong><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with C, Java, Kotlin, Objective-C, Swift, JavaScript, Python or Bash, and ideally ARM/ARM64 assembly.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Security Research:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Awareness of emerging security technologies, Cloud security, and developments in mobile operating systems, APIs, tools, and security libraries.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">What to expect from our hiring process</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><stron