<p><strong>Why this role matters</strong><br>In your first year, you will drive growth and strengthen Flora Food Group's position as the leading provider of plant-based spreads in the Austrian and Swiss market.<br>This role is essential to advancing our mission of offering healthy, sustainable, and affordable alternatives to dairy.<br>You will actively manage key accounts, ensuring forecast accuracy and developing negotiation strategies that unlock value.<br>Your work will directly influence how our products reach kitchens across Austria, supporting better food choices for consumers.</p>
<p><strong>What you'll do</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Manage major Swiss accounts, actively understanding and responding to customer needs and expectations.</li>
<li>Control and ensure accuracy of sales forecasts to support business planning.</li>
<li>Plan and oversee customer budgets to align with growth objectives.</li>
<li>Develop and implement negotiation strategies that deliver value-adding measures in 2027.</li>
<li>Drive growth strategies with key customers to elevate Flora's market presence.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Performance</strong><br>You will own the accuracy of forecasts and the execution of growth plans, directly impacting sales volume and market share in Switzerland.<br>Success will be measured by your ability to manage risks and opportunities in customer business and to implement effective negotiation strategies.<br>Your data-driven approach will ensure that Flora remains a step ahead in a competitive market.</p>
<p><strong>Care</strong><br>You will report to the Head of Sales CHATIT and collaborate closely with Sales Leads, Finance, Demand Planning, and Marketing teams.<br>Working within a dynamic team, you will contribute to a culture that values shared success and entrepreneurial spirit.<br>Your decisions will reflect long-term thinking, balancing immediate business needs with sustainable growth.</p>
<p><strong>Passion</strong><br>You are passionate about plant-based food and the role it plays in healthier, more sustainable diets.<br>You bring curiosity about consumer trends and a commitment to raising the bar in how Flora's products meet taste, nutrition, and functionality expectations.<br>Your enthusiasm for food innovation will inspire your approach to account management and market development.</p>
<p><strong>About you</strong><br>You have a strong background in key account management within the fast-moving consumer goods sector, with experience in the Swiss retail and food service markets.<br>You are skilled in using data tools such as Excel, Nielsen, and GfK to inform your decisions and strategies.<br>Your negotiation skills are proven, with a track record of implementing sustainable growth strategies with major customers.<br>You thrive in a role that offers autonomy and the chance to shape negotiation approaches and business development.<br>You are fluent in German and English and comfortable working in a hybrid environment.<br>You are genuinely interested in food culture and curious about how consumer behaviour and future food trends shape innovation.<br>You understand that strong brands are built by anticipating what's next in taste, nutrition and functionality, and by translating insight into meaningful consumer experiences.</p>
<p><strong>Where this could lead to</strong><br>This role typically leads to a Senior Key Account Manager or Key Account Teamlead position, where you will take on greater responsibility for strategic accounts and broader market influence.<br>Growth into this role usually occurs as you demonstrate success in driving business development and negotiation outcomes over time.</p>
<p><strong>What's next</strong><br>If this opportunity sounds exciting, we'd love to hear from you.</p>
