on day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we hire</h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening call (30 min)</strong> with our VP Engineering. It's two-way: ask us anything, including the hard questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical deep-dive call</strong>: walk us through something you built from scratch, the decisions you made and what went wrong.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet Scalera Day</strong>: come to our office in Zürich, work on a real problem with real (anonymized) construction documents, and meet the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer</strong>: if it's a fit on both sides, we'll move quickly to an offer.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Working at Scalera</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zürich HQ, four days in the office, Fridays remote</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Occasional customer visits across Switzerland, Austria and Germany</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Small team, no bureaucracy. You'll work directly with the CEO, CTO, VP Engineering and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary and equity</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founders and former founders:</strong> if you're unsure whether you fit, send a few lines about what you built and why you moved on. We read every one.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/scalera/senior-backend-ai-engineer-zurich-301606","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793828415},{"slug":"senior-ai-ml-engineer-zurich-21808","company_name":"Scalera","title":"Senior AI/ML Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role is also open to candidates living in the EU or EEA. We can't consider applications from other locations.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>If you've built something before, start here</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most ML jobs hand you a benchmark. This one hands you a business problem with paying customers and their real data. Construction tenders are long, messy and full of trade jargon, and every decision a customer makes on our platform becomes a labeled example you can train on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We need someone who can turn that data into models that customers notice: from the first experiment to the model serving production traffic, and back again when a customer says it got something wrong. If you've founded a company (whether it worked out or not), been the first ML engineer somewhere, or shipped a model people paid for, this role was written for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About Scalera</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scalera is an ETH Zurich spin-off building AI for the €200B+ European construction industry. Manufacturers, wholesalers and suppliers in Switzerland, Austria and Germany still run their most document-heavy work by hand, from reading 300-page tenders to retyping purchase orders into their ERP. We automate that work one process at a time, and ML sits at the center of every one of them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll own</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the ML behind our products, end to end. In practice that means:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training and fine-tuning</strong>: embedding models, rerankers, classifiers and LLMs, trained on our own data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Document understanding</strong>: models that pull structure, quantities and product specs out of tenders, orders and catalogs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product matching</strong>: retrieval and LLM agents that match tender positions to the right products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evaluation</strong>: offline benchmarks, per-customer evals and gates that keep a new model from shipping if it makes things worse.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training and serving infrastructure</strong>: automated retrain pipelines, GPU serving and vector search in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer problems</strong>: when a model gets something wrong for a customer, finding out why and fixing it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What success looks like after 3 months</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">There's a model or part of the pipeline people now think of as yours, and you're the one deciding what happens to it next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've spotted a problem nobody asked you to solve, made the case for it, and shipped a first version.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A model you trained runs in production, and customers can see the difference in their results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retraining runs automatically, and nothing reaches customers without passing an eval you designed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've cut LLM cost or latency by replacing an expensive step with a smaller model of your own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've decided at least one thing we should stop building.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>You'll probably thrive here if</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've taken something from zero to one: a company, a model in production, or a side project with real users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've trained and fine-tuned models yourself, ideally embeddings, retrieval or document models, and evaluated them honestly on held-out data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built with LLMs in production and know where agents fail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write strong Python and can run what you build: Docker, CI/CD, and cloud on GCP, AWS or Azure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You measure before you believe, and a single aggregate score doesn't convince you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather open a customer's actual document than wait for a spec.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with ambiguity. You can make progress while the problem is still half-defined, which at a startup it usually is.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a large scope of responsibility and are happy to own things well beyond your job title.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rapidly changing requirements don't throw you. When customers or priorities shift, you adapt and keep going.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy direct customer contact and want to be on customer calls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write clearly in English. German is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>You probably won't enjoy it if</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You just want to code and go home.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't like talking to customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ambiguity and chaos bother you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a well-defined research agenda handed to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather hand a model to someone else to deploy and debug.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your main goal is managing people soon. Here, scope grows with what you own, not with headcount.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our stack</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python and PyTorch, open-weight and frontier LLMs, LangGraph, Langfuse, PostgreSQL with pgvector, Pinecone, and GCP. You don't need to know all of it on day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we hire</h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening call (30 min)</strong> with our VP Engineering. It's two-way: ask us anything, including the hard questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical deep-dive call</strong>: walk us through a model or system you built, the decisions you made and what went wrong in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet Scalera Day</strong>: come to our office in Zürich, work on a real problem with real (anonymized) tender data, and meet the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer</strong>: if it's a fit on both sides, we'll move quickly to an offer.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Working at Scalera</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zürich HQ, four days in the office, Fridays remote. If not located in Zürich then this role is open to remote within the EU or EEA,</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Occasional customer visits across Switzerland, Austria and Germany</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Small team, no bureaucracy. You'll work directly with the CEO, CTO, VP Engineering and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary and meaningful equity</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founders and former founders:</strong> if you're unsure whether you fit, send a few lines about what you built and why you moved on. We read every one.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/scalera/senior-ai-ml-engineer-zurich-21808","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793828415},{"slug":"account-executive-dach-amsterdam-123797","company_name":"Tellent","title":"Account Executive  - DACH","description":"<h4>About the Role</h4><p>We're building the sales engine for Tellent HR in the DACH market, and we're looking for an Account Executive to help us do it. Think of it as joining a startup inside a scale-up.</p><p>First and foremost, this is a hands-on selling role. You'll own the full sales cycle for Tellent HR (Manage and/or Grow), split roughly 80/20 between new business and expansion into our existing customer base. Inbound isn't going to be your main pipeline driver, so expect to spend around 50% of your time prospecting, against ambitious daily and weekly activity targets. Alongside that, you'll help us work out <em>how</em> we win in DACH: testing motions fast and doubling down on what drives revenue.</p><p>You'll work with a dedicated Product Marketing Manager and Customer Success Manager in the Tellent HR squad. CS capacity is limited, though, so you'll run deals independently, including demos and follow-through.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Your 12-Month Journey</h4><ul><li><p><strong>First 3 months:</strong> Learn Tellent HR, our ideal customers and the competitive landscape in DACH. Build your first pipeline through outbound, establish a consistent daily activity rhythm, and close your first deals.</p></li><li><p><strong>Within 6 months:</strong> Consistently hit your activity, pipeline and revenue targets, understand which sales motions work best in the DACH market, and feed insights back to Product Marketing and Product.</p></li><li><p><strong>After 1 year:</strong> Be the go-to expert on selling Tellent HR in DACH, with a repeatable, data-backed playbook that others can pick up.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What You'll Be Doing</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Own the full sales cycle, independently:</strong> Run 1–3 month, multi-stakeholder deals involving HR leaders, founders/CEOs and Finance, from first touch through to close and follow-through.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hunt for new pipeline (around 50% of your time):</strong> Prospect by phone, email and LinkedIn, consistently hit your daily and weekly activity targets, and maintain 3–4x pipeline coverage. Partner, CS and marketing leads are a bonus, not the plan.</p></li><li><p><strong>Drive expansion:</strong> Prospect into existing Tellent customers to cross-sell and upsell, e.g. Recruitee customers adding Tellent HR, or Manage customers adding Grow.</p></li><li><p><strong>Sell on value:</strong> Run consultative discovery and tailored demos, position on business outcomes, and handle objections, including against key competitors (with support from PMM).</p></li><li><p><strong>Manage deals with discipline:</strong> Use mutual action plans, keep HubSpot accurate (including SPICED), forecast reliably and disqualify early.</p></li><li><p><strong>Test and build, alongside selling:</strong> Experiment with sales motions, sequences and verticals, help build the playbook with our PMM, and bring customer and competitive insights from the DACH market back to Product and Marketing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>What You Bring</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Early-stage DNA:</strong> You've sold in a startup or early scale-up and built pipeline and processes where none existed. You know what it means to be an early sales hire.</p></li><li><p><strong>Proven hunter:</strong> A track record of self-generating pipeline through outbound and consistently hitting ambitious activity targets. You genuinely enjoy picking up the phone and creating opportunities from scratch.</p></li><li><p><strong>B2B SaaS sales experience:</strong> You've closed new business (ideally expansion too) as a fully autonomous AE in a startup or early scale-up, running 1–5 month, multi-stakeholder sales cycles. HR tech experience is a plus, not essential.</p></li><li><p><strong>Self-sufficient and resilient:</strong> You don't wait for leads, support teams or perfect processes. You bounce back from rejection and stay disciplined through the ups and downs of building something new.</p></li><li><p><strong>Consultativ