&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/nebius/service-desk-l3-it-operations-technical-lead-amsterdam-139561","tags":["IT Operations"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793948121},{"slug":"devops-engineer-amsterdam-449903","company_name":"SkinVision","title":"DevOps Engineer","description":"<p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">For this role, we will only consider candidates who are currently based in the Netherlands.</span></span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">About SkinVision</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Skin cancer is highly treatable when caught early, but limited access to specialist care and long wait times delay diagnosis, increasing the risk of late-stage cases and driving up treatment costs. SkinVision, founded in Amsterdam in 2012, exists to close that gap. Our proprietary AI — certified as a Class IIa medical device under EU regulation, with over 90% sensitivity and 89% specificity — has already helped nearly 3 million people worldwide detect early signs of skin cancer. Today, SkinVision has a database of more than 6 million skin spot assessments and can reach 20 million people through insurer partnerships. High-risk cases are reviewed by a team of dermatologists, who support users in taking the right next step — from urgent care to a specialist referral. We are extending this further, connecting users faster to the specialist care they need. We're a focused, international team, active globally, united by one goal: making early detection accessible to everyone, everywhere. If you join us, you're not just building a product — you're helping close the gap between a person noticing something and getting the care they need.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">DevOps at SkinVision</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As a DevOps Engineer at SkinVision, you will play a key role in building, scaling, and securing the infrastructure that powers our AI-driven health platform. You’ll design and maintain our cloud-based systems in AWS, implement CI/CD pipelines, enhance observability using Datadog, and drive operational excellence through automation and monitoring.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Your work will directly impact the reliability and scalability of a medical-grade system that serves users globally. You’ll collaborate closely with backend, ML, and product teams to ensure smooth delivery, rapid deployments, and resilient operations — ultimately enabling us to deliver life-saving technology with confidence.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Beyond hands-on expertise with AWS and modern DevOps tooling, we’re looking for someone who thinks architecturally. You’ll get to know our current setup, form your own view of how it should evolve, and help define a target vision for our infrastructure, then drive its implementation. Day-to-day operational work is part of the role, but we value someone who thinks before building and takes ownership of where our infrastructure goes next.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">What you will do</span></span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Cloud Infrastructure &amp; Automation</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design, build, and manage AWS-based infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, and cost efficiency.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Implement and manage infrastructure as code (IaC) using tools like Terraform or CloudFormation.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Automate environment provisioning, configuration, and deployments using CI/CD pipelines.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ensure system resilience, security, and performance through automated monitoring and alerting.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">CI/CD &amp; Deployment</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design and optimize CI/CD pipelines to support rapid, reliable, and safe deployments across environments.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Manage deployment workflows using Argo CD and Kubernetes.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Collaborate with developers and ML engineers to streamline build, test, and release processes.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Integrate automated testing, rollback strategies, and version control into the deployment lifecycle.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Observability &amp; Monitoring</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Build a comprehensive observability stack using Datadog for metrics, logs, traces, and alerts.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define service-level objectives (SLOs), service-level indicators (SLIs), and dashboards for system performance.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Proactively detect and resolve performance bottlenecks, capacity issues, and reliability risks.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Create automated health checks and ensure visibility across production systems.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Security &amp; Compliance</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Implement security best practices for AWS, containers, and CI/CD pipelines.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Manage identity, access, and secret handling (IAM, Secrets Manager, Parameter Store).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ensure compliance with medical device standards and data privacy regulations (GDPR, HIPAA).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Partner with the Information Security Officer to embed security controls across infrastructure and deployments.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Reliability &amp; Incident Management</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Lead incident response and root cause analysis for infrastructure or deployment-related issues.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Establish SLAs and operational runbooks for production environments.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Continuously improve system reliability through chaos testing, redundancy, and fault tolerance.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Mentor engineers on DevOps principles, observability practices, and infrastructure automation.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Infrastructure Strategy &amp; Architecture</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Assess the current infrastructure and deployment setup, and form a well-reasoned view of how it should evolve.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define and maintain a target architecture for our cloud platform, balancing reliability, scalability, security, and cost.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Translate the target vision into a practical roadmap and drive its implementation incrementally, alongside day-to-day operations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Document and communicate architectural decisions, aligning with engineering and leadership on technical direction.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Essential skills</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Minimum of 6 years of experience in DevOps, Site Reliability Engineering, or Cloud Infrastructure roles.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong expertise with AWS services (EC2, ECS/EKS, S3, RDS, CloudWatch, Lambda, etc.).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Expert in Kubernetes and Argo CD, deploying and managing production-grade custom Helm charts with secure, automated GitOps workflows in EKS</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Advanced knowledge of CI/CD systems (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Jenkins, or similar).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Proficiency in Datadog for observability, monitoring, and alerting.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong scripting and automation skills in Python, Bash, or Go.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience managing infrastructure with Terraform, CloudFormation, or Ansible.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with networking fundamentals, load balancing, and API gateway configuration.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Excellent problem-solving and incident management skills.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Desirable skills</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience in regulated industries such as healthcare, MedTech, or FinTech.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with multi-environment architecture (staging, pre-prod, production) and blue-green deployments.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Exposure to event-driven systems, message queues, and data streaming (Kafka, SNS/SQS).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Understanding of Zero Trust networking and cloud security best practices.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience in cost optimization and performance tuning in AWS.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Qualifications</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent experience).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Certifications such as AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, Kubernetes Administrator (CKA), or Terraform Associate are a plus.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">What we offer</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A competitive salary, additional benefits, and a hybrid working policy</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A vibrant, dynamic, and rapidly growing scale-up in Amsterdam</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">An enthusiastic, professional, and international team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Regular team events, including off-sites and fun activities</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Unlimited skin checks for you</span></p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skinvision/devops-engineer-amsterdam-449903","tags":["Product Development"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946684},{"slug":"senior-ux-designer-amsterdam-229420","company_name":"SkinVision","title":"Senior UX Designer","description":"<p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">For this role, we will only consider candidates who are currently based in the Netherlands.</span></span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">About SkinVision</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Skin cancer is highly treatable when caught early, but limited access to specialist care and long wait times delay diagnosis, increasing the risk of late-stage cases and driving up treatment costs. SkinVision, founded in Amsterdam in 2012, exists to close that gap. Our proprietary AI — certified as a Class IIa medical device under EU regulation, with over 90% sensitivity and 89% specificity — has already helped nearly 3 million people worldwide detect early signs of skin cancer. Today, SkinVision has a database of more than 6 million skin spot assessments and can reach 20 million people through insurer partnerships. High-risk cases are reviewed by a team of dermatologists, who support users in taking the right next step — from urgent care to a specialist referral. We are extending this further, connecting users faster to the specialist care they need. We're a focused, international team, active globally, united by one goal: making early detection accessible to everyone, everywhere. If you join us, you're not just building a product — you're helping close the gap between a person noticing something and getting the care they need.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">Senior UX Designer at SkinVision</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">As a Senior UX Designer, you will be responsible for designing and refining intuitive, engaging, and effective user experiences across SkinVision’s digital products. You will conduct user research, create wireframes and prototypes, and work closely with cross-functional teams to ensure our platform provides the best possible user experience. Your work will directly contribute to making early skin cancer detection accessible and user-friendly.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">Your impact</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Enhance User Experience: Design seamless, user-friendly interfaces that encourage engagement and retention.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Optimize User Flows: Improve onboarding and interaction flows to make early skin cancer detection more intuitive.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Data-Driven Design: Leverage user insights and testing to refine and iterate designs for maximum impact.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Cross-Functional Collaboration: Work closely with product, engineering, and marketing teams to align design with business goals.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Drive Innovation: Experiment with new design methodologies to enhance accessibility and engagement in digital healthcare</span>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">What you will do</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">User Research &amp; Insights</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Conduct and analyze user research to understand behaviors, needs, and pain points.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Employ surveys, interviews, usability testing, and analytics to validate design decisions.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">Wireframing, Prototyping, and Design</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Create wireframes, low/high-fidelity prototypes, and user flows for web and mobile applications.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Iterate designs based on user testing and data insights.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">Collaboration &amp; Implementation</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Work closely with developers to ensure smooth implementation of designs.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Participate in product meetings, ensuring UX is a key consideration in feature development.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">Design Strategy &amp; Branding</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Align design choices with SkinVision’s brand identity and business goals.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Maintain design consistency across platforms and devices.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">Usability Testing &amp; Optimization</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Conduct usability testing sessions to validate and refine designs.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Analyze user behavior using heatmaps, analytics, and A/B testing to improve user experience.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#121317">Design Documentation &amp; Systems</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Maintain UX guidelines, design systems, and component libraries for consistency across products.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Document user flows, personas, and interaction models to guide product development.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">We are looking for someone who</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Thinks User-First: You are deeply committed to designing experiences that prioritize user needs and engagement.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Has an Eye for Detail: You ensure that every interaction and visual element is polished and user-friendly.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Is Data-Informed: You make design decisions based on user research, testing, and analytics.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Loves Problem-Solving: You enjoy tackling UX challenges and iterating to create the best experience possible.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Works Well in a Team: You thrive in a collaborative environment, working closely with product, engineering, and marketing teams.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Essential Skills</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">6-8 years of UX design experience, preferably in healthtech, SaaS, or native and reach native mobile applications.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong proficiency in Figma, Adobe XD, or other design tools.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong proficiency in using tools such as Claude Design, Claude Code, adobe cc, Lovable, or similar.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience conducting user research and usability testing.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong understanding of interaction design, information architecture, and accessibility principles.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ability to collaborate with cross-functional teams and translate business goals into effective design solutions.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Strong communication and presentation skills for articulating design rationale.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience or an understanding of design in HealthTech OR experience working in highly regulated product environments.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Desirable Skills</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience in digital health or medtech.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Knowledge of design thinking methodologies.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with analytics tools (Google Analytics, Mixpanel, Hotjar) to inform UX decisions.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience working with design systems and component libraries.</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A degree in UX/UI Design, Human-Computer Interaction, Psychology, or a related field is preferred.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">What we offer</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A competitive salary, additional benefits, and a hybrid working policy</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A vibrant, dynamic, and rapidly growing scale-up in Amsterdam</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">An enthusiastic, professional, and international team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Regular team events, including off-sites and fun activities</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Unlimited skin checks for you</span></p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skinvision/senior-ux-designer-amsterdam-229420","tags":["Product Development"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946684},{"slug":"senior-growth-marketing-manager-rotterdam-462174","company_name":"AIHR","title":"Senior Growth Marketing Manager","description":"<p><span style="color:#000000">Are you an ambitious growth marketer with an entrepreneurial spirit and a track record of scaling customer acquisition? Do you love diving into data, spotting opportunities, and turning ideas into measurable growth? Are you excited by opening new acquisition channels and finding smarter ways to grow in an AI-driven world?</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">AIHR is looking for an experienced Senior Growth Marketing Manager</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> to help accelerate growth across our B2C and B2B businesses. You'll work across the entire acquisition funnel, from scaling paid media and improving conversion to launching new growth initiatives that drive MQLs and revenue.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You'll join an ambitious, results-driven Growth Marketing team, working closely with our specialists to challenge existing approaches, experiment with new ideas, and deliver results. You'll have the autonomy to lead initiatives, the support of an experienced team, and the opportunity to make a direct impact on a global e-learning business.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About AIHR</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Founded in 2016 with the mission to future-proof HR, the </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.aihr.com/"><span style="color:#1155CC">Academy to Innovate HR (AIHR)</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> has become the world’s market leader in online training for human resources (HR) professionals. We have a global customer base spread across 140+ countries, amongst which companies like Unilever, Reckitt, Goldman Sachs, Philips, Deloitte, Nike, Heineken, and UBS. It is our goal to continuously upskill and empower 1,000,000 HR Professionals.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are an international team of 100+ people, driven by excellence, innovation, and a hunger to grow in everything we do. As such, we strive to provide the world’s best courses and excellent support to our customers while continuously optimizing every aspect of our work. With over 30 nationalities, our team is diverse, yet we all share a few traits: we're friendly, enthusiastic, and great team players.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Being a fast-growing company, working at AIHR means taking on a lot of responsibility and getting countless opportunities to develop yourself in new areas and the potential to craft your own role.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Role and Responsibilities</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As our Senior Growth Marketing Manager, you'll play a key role in accelerating customer acquisition across our B2C and B2B businesses. Working closely with the Head of Growth Marketing and VP of Marketing, you'll help us achieve our ambitious growth targets, improve acquisition efficiency, and identify new opportunities to scale.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">A core part of your role will be diving into performance data to understand what's working, what's not, and where our biggest growth opportunities lie. You'll work closely with our Performance Marketing Specialist to scale paid acquisition, challenge existing strategies, test new approaches, and support campaign execution where needed. You'll also collaborate with our CRO Specialist to identify opportunities across landing pages, website journeys, and conversion funnels, turning insights into experiments that drive more leads and revenue.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You'll bring a strong growth perspective to our email marketing efforts, working with the team to analyze nurture flows, promotional campaigns, and audience segments, and identify opportunities to improve performance. Beyond optimizing existing channels, you'll explore, launch, and scale new acquisition opportunities, including those emerging from the changing AI- and LLM-driven marketing landscape.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Most importantly, this is a hands-on role where you'll do more than develop strategies and bring ideas to the table. You'll actively execute initiatives yourself or work closely with the wider team to bring them to life. Whether you're launching a new campaign, testing an acquisition channel, or improving conversion, you'll take ownership of turning opportunities into measurable business results.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">On a typical week</span></strong><br></p><p><span style="color:#000000">It's Monday morning, and you start the week with a coffee and a look at last week's acquisition performance. You open GA4, HubSpot, and your marketing dashboards to see how we're tracking against our B2C and B2B MQL targets. While digging into the data, you notice that one of our paid campaigns is generating plenty of traffic, but conversions have dropped. You investigate further, identify a few potential causes, and head into the Growth Marketing stand-up with some ideas to improve performance.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">After the stand-up, you catch up with our Performance Marketing Specialist to review campaign performance and discuss opportunities to scale. You identify a promising new audience and agree to test a different creative approach. Rather than just handing over your ideas, you jump into the advertising platform to help set up the campaign and work with the team to get the new creatives ready for launch.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On Tuesday, you're focused on improving our B2B acquisition funnel. You've spotted an opportunity to increase conversions on the AI for HR Boot Camp landing page. You meet with our B2B Marketer and CRO Specialist to review the data, discuss your hypothesis, and agree on an experiment. You brief the team, align with sales on the proposed changes, and help move the experiment towards launch.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Wednesday is a work-from-home day, giving you time to dive deeper into our acquisition strategy. You've been exploring how AI and LLMs are changing the way HR professionals discover training providers. You identify a potential new acquisition opportunity, research the market, and put together a practical plan to test it. Later, you meet with the Head of Growth Marketing to challenge your assumptions, refine the approach, and agree on the next steps.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On Thursday, you review the performance of our B2C email nurture flows with the Email Marketing team. You notice an opportunity to improve conversions from leads to MQLs and propose a change to the messaging and sequence. After lunch with colleagues in the office, you turn your attention to an upcoming quarterly campaign, working with the wider Marketing team to finalize the messaging and coordinate the launch. You also start investigating new channels that could help expand the campaign's reach and attract new audiences.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Friday starts with reviewing the results of a recent landing page experiment. The changes have improved conversion, so you work with the CRO Specialist to roll them out more broadly. You also catch up with our BizOps team to improve HubSpot reporting, ensuring we have better visibility into acquisition performance and opportunities for growth. Before wrapping up the week, you review progress against our growth priorities, share your findings with the team, and identify the next opportunities worth pursuing.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">After a productive week of analyzing, experimenting, and driving initiatives forward, you close your laptop and join your colleagues for Friday drinks.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">We offer</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A revenue-generating role in a fast-growing scale-up company;&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Competitive, benchmarked compensation;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A high degree of autonomy in a vibrant, result-driven, inclusive, and international team;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">A beautiful office right across Rotterdam Central Station (Milleniumtower) and a satellite office in Amsterdam;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">26 paid holidays per year + 1 extra day for the first 5 years you work at AIHR</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Exchange any 2 public holiday days for 2 other days of your choice;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Work from anywhere policy, where you can work abroad for 20 days in a calendar year;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Pension plan;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">4 Trust days per year (ad-hoc recovery days to take whenever you're overwhelmed, exhausted, or need to deal with something personal);</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#0E101A">Access to OpenUp mental health platform;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Personal development budget, training, and we pay for the books you read;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">All public transport expenses covered (NS Business Card);</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">MacBook + all other equipment you need to do your work;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Daily lunch prepared by a chef, weekly drinks, and fun team activities;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Free access to the office gym.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">Get a taste of AIHR experience and check out our </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://aihr.recruitee.com/benefits-guide"><span style="color:#1155CC">AIHR Benefits Guide</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000">!</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you are</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We're looking for an ambitious, data-driven, and commercially minded growth marketer with an entrepreneurial spirit. Someone who loves identifying opportunities, challenging existing approaches, and turning ideas into measurable results. You're not just a strategic thinker; you're equally excited about getting operational, executing ideas yourself, and making things happen.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You have:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">8+ years of experience in growth marketing, with a proven track record of scaling customer acquisition, ideally across both B2C and B2B businesses in SaaS, e-learning, or other high-growth industries;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Demonstrable experience scaling paid acquisition campaigns, including managing or scaling advertising budgets of €100,000+ per month;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to dive into performance data, identify growth opportunities, and translate insights into actionable initiatives;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A strong understanding of full-funnel marketing, including paid acquisition, CRO, landing page optimization, email marketing, and growth economics such as CAC and LTV;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Strong experience with HubSpot or comparable CRM platforms, including segmentation, automation, lifecycle marketing, attribution, and reporting;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience identifying, testing, and scaling new acquisition channels and growth opportunities;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Strong AI proficiency, with experience using ChatGPT and Claude to analyze data, improve workflows, and accelerate execution;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An understanding of how AI and LLMs are changing customer acquisition, with a forward-thinking approach to emerging marketing channels;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A proactive, hands-on approach, with the ability to independently lead and execute initiatives while collaborating effectively with the wider team;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with a collaborative mindset, openness to feedback, and a hunger to grow;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Bonus:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Experience in event marketing, community-led growth, or account-based marketing (ABM).</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Apply for the job</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Are you excited to become our new Senior Growth Marketing Manager? Then we'd love to hear from you! We are looking to hire for this role as soon as we find an eligible candidate.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">P.S. </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">Research shows that while men apply to jobs when they meet an average of 60% of the criteria, women tend to apply only when they meet 100% of them. So if you think you have what it takes, but don't necessarily meet every single point above, please still apply. We'd love to consider you and see if you could be a great fit.&nbsp;</span></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aihr/senior-growth-marketing-manager-rotterdam-462174","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946684},{"slug":"senior-php-backend-developer-zoetermeer-85077","company_name":"SHIFTBASE B.V.","title":"Senior PHP Backend Developer","description":"<h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">About Shiftbase</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">At Shiftbase, we build workforce software that helps people get work done. Thousands of teams across Europe rely on our platform every day to plan work, track time, and manage leave, freeing them from unnecessary admin so they can focus on what matters and what sparked their business.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">As we continue to grow in customers, usage and product ambition, the demands on our platform grow with us. Our backend needs to scale in </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">quality, reliability and speed of change</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">. That’s why we’re investing heavily in modernising our platform, building a foundation that allows us to move faster, deliver better experiences, and support the next phase of Shiftbase’s growth.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">About the role:</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317"><br>As a Senior Backend Engineer, you are a key driver of both product delivery and platform modernisation. You work on the core of our backend, improving reliability, performance and scalability, with the explicit goal of turning Shiftbase from a platform people enjoy into a platform they love.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">You help evolve a mature monolithic codebase into a more modular, testable and future-proof architecture. By modernising the foundation of the product, you directly enable better user experiences, faster iteration and higher overall product quality.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">What you'll do</span></h3><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Drive technical excellence</span></strong></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design and deliver high-quality, scalable solutions for complex features and system components</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Make informed architectural decisions that balance pragmatism with long-term vision</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Set the bar for technical craft through your contributions and code reviews</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Own complex technical initiatives from design through production, breaking them into testable increments</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Build for reliability and scale</span></strong></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define comprehensive testing strategies for complex features, championing quality within the team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Debug and resolve complex issues across multiple components, improving system observability</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Apply security best practices throughout the development lifecycle</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Contribute to monitoring, alerting and system health improvements</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Enable team growth</span></strong></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Mentor engineers with targeted technical guidance and feedback</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support onboarding and enable a collaborative, knowledge-sharing environment</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Help shape delivery practices and improve team velocity through data-informed decisions</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">What we're looking for</span></h3><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Core technical expertise</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">You have deep backend engineering experience with complex, high-scale systems. We don't expect expertise in everything listed below. We value engineers who've built depth and breadth through genuine curiosity and a drive to solve real problems. These are examples of competencies that matter in this role:</span></p><ul class="ak-ul"><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Modern PHP &amp; architectural patterns</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Experience with hexagonal architecture, domain-driven design, or similar patterns that emphasize domain modeling over framework magic. You can build maintainable systems without relying on framework shortcuts.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">SQL &amp; database design</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Comfort writing raw SQL (not just ORM abstractions) and working with complex relational schemas particularly around time-sensitive data like scheduling, timesheets and payroll where integrity and performance are critical.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Legacy modernisation experience</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: You've gradually evolved mature systems rather than pursuing big-bang rewrites. You know when to modernize strategically vs. leaving working code untouched, and understand the balance between progress and stability when serving thousands of customers.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Monolith to services</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Experience breaking down monoliths with good judgment about when distribution solves real problems (deployment bottlenecks, team autonomy) vs. when it adds unnecessary complexity.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Testing in legacy contexts</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: Practical experience with unit and integration testing, particularly incrementally improving coverage in existing systems.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">This might be your dream job if…</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You enjoy </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">modernising a mature platform</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> and turning legacy code into something you’re proud of</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You get energy from </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">breaking down a monolith</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> and shaping a more modular, service-oriented architecture</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You care about </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">product quality</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, not just “shipping code”.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You like improving reliability, performance and developer experience as much as adding new features</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">✅ You enjoy working closely with product and frontend to make better technical and product decisions</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">This probably isn’t your dream job if…</span></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You only want to work on </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">greenfield projects</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> and avoid legacy systems altogether</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You’re uncomfortable refactoring existing code or making incremental improvements</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You prefer being handed fully-defined solutions rather than helping shape them</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You’re looking for a role where architecture decisions are already “done”</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">⛔️ You’d rather optimise locally than care about the </span><strong><span style="color:#121317">end-to-end product experience</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Note: Candidates outside the Netherlands will not be considered</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/shiftbase-bv/senior-php-backend-developer-zoetermeer-85077","tags":["IT / Engineering"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Zoetermeer, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"wo-stage-onderzoek-milieukosten-mbv-bestaande-afval-en-emissiestatistieken-den-haag-201330","company_name":"Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek","title":"wo-stage onderzoek milieukosten m.b.v. bestaande afval- en emissiestatistieken","description":"<h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">wo-</span><span style="color:#0580A1">afstudeerstage/praktijkstage, </span><span style="color:#271D6C">vanaf februari 2027</span></span></strong></h4><p><em><span style="font-size:1.2em">Ben jij die nieuwsgierige onderzoeker die energie krijgt van data, duurzaamheid en nieuwe inzichten?<br>Wil jij een inhoudelijke bijdrage leveren aan de statistieken van het CBS?</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">uitdaging</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Het kabinet wil dat Nederland in 2050 volledig circulair is. Om te kunnen volgen of we die doelstelling halen, is betrouwbare informatie nodig over onder andere afval en emissies naar water. Het CBS verzamelt en publiceert deze gegevens voor bedrijven. Daarbij maken we vooral gebruik van gegevens uit het elektronisch Milieujaarverslag (e-MJV), aangevuld met enquêtes.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Naast de hoeveelheid afval en wateremissies brengen we ook de milieukosten van bedrijven in kaart, bijvoorbeeld de kosten voor afvalverwerking en voor het lozen van afvalwater. Hiervoor wordt nu een aparte enquête gebruikt. Maar is dat eigenlijk wel nodig?</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Tijdens je stage onderzoek je of we de milieukosten voor afval en wateremissies kunnen berekenen met gegevens die al beschikbaar zijn. Je combineert bijvoorbeeld gegevens over de hoeveelheid afval en geloosd water met bestaande indicatoren, zoals gemiddelde kosten per ton afval en sectorspecifieke kosten per kubieke meter geloosd water.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je gaat onder andere:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">bestaande data en indicatoren analyseren en beoordelen op bruikbaarheid;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">onderzoeken welke methode het meest geschikt is om de milieukosten te schatten;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">een berekening of model ontwikkelen waarmee de kosten kunnen worden afgeleid;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">de uitkomsten vergelijken met de beschikbare gegevens uit de huidige enquête;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">onderzoeken hoe betrouwbaar en bruikbaar de schattingen zijn;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">je bevindingen vertalen naar een concreet advies voor het CBS.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Met jouw onderzoek willen we bepalen of we meer uit bestaande data kunnen halen en minder hoeven uit te vragen bij bedrijven. Als blijkt dat de milieukosten betrouwbaar kunnen worden berekend, kunnen de uitkomsten bovendien worden gebruikt om de bestaande afval- en waterstatistieken te controleren.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">In het meest gunstige scenario kan de aparte enquête naar milieukosten gedeeltelijk of helemaal vervallen. Dat betekent minder administratieve lasten voor bedrijven, efficiënter gebruik van beschikbare data en mogelijk betrouwbaardere statistieken.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">stageplek </span><span style="color:#271D6C">bij CBS </span><span style="color:#0580A1">Den Haag</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">We verwelkomen je binnen de sector Leefomgeving bij team Milieu. Met 20 gedreven professionals werken we aan milieu gerelateerde statistieken en doen we onderzoek naar actuele thema’s zoals klimaat(verandering) en circulaire economie. We werken nauw samen met andere teams binnen het CBS.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">We werken hard aan het continu verbeteren van onze statistieken en de cijfers beschikbaar te stellen voor het publiek. Voorbeelden van recente publicaties uit ons team zijn:</span></p><ul><li><p><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.cbs.nl/nl-nl/nieuws/2026/02/bedrijven-investeerden-in-2024-minder-in-milieu"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Bedrijven investeerden in 2024 minder in milieu | CBS</span></a></p></li><li><p><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.cbs.nl/nl-nl/nieuws/2022/50/bijna-2-procent-meer-bedrijfs-en-industrieafval-in-2021"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Bijna 2 procent meer bedrijfs- en industrieafval in 2021 | CBS</span></a></p></li><li><p><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://opendata.cbs.nl/#/CBS/nl/dataset/82863NED/table?dl=E7F90"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Milieukosten en -investeringen van bedrijven | CBS</span></a></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit breng </span><span style="color:#0580A1">jij</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> mee</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je volgt een wo-opleiding milieukunde, economie, technische bestuurskunde, data science of een aanverwante opleiding.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je hebt affiniteit met het onderwerp circulaire economie.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je bent&nbsp;analytisch sterk en kunt complexe vraagstukken gestructureerd onderzoeken en vertalen naar heldere inzichten.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je kunt goed programmeren in R.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je bent sociaal en communicatief vaardig en kunt je ideeën en bevindingen helder overbrengen aan verschillende gesprekspartners.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Omdat tijdens de stage alle communicatie – zowel mondeling als schriftelijk – in het Nederlands plaatsvindt, is een goede beheersing van de Nederlandse taal noodzakelijk.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit kun je van </span><span style="color:#0580A1">ons</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> verwachten</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een fijne leeromgeving waarin je:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw competenties in kwantitatieve data-analyse versterkt door gebruik te maken van milieustatistieken en economische databronnen;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw onderzoeksvaardigheden aanscherpt op het gebied van de circulaire economie en levenscyclusanalyse;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw programmeervaardigheden in R verder ontwikkelt;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">ervaring opdoet met het interpreteren van verschillende datasets om betrouwbare profielen op te stellen.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Voor jouw inzet ontvang je een stagevergoeding van € 800 bruto per maand (op basis van 40 uur per week).</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Samen met je stagebegeleider stem je af hoe je hybride kunt werken, met flexibele werktijden en de optie om deels vanuit huis aan jouw stageopdracht te werken.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit zijn </span><span style="color:#0580A1">onze</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> voorwaarden</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Het betreft een stageopdracht en geen werkervaringsplek. Voordat je aan de stage begint verwachten we dat je vanuit de onderwijsinstelling een stagebegeleider hebt, waarmee de stage is afgestemd en concrete leerdoelen zijn afgesproken. <br>Deze stageopdracht is bedoeld voor studenten die momenteel staan ingeschreven bij een onderwijsinstelling; afgestudeerden komen niet in aanmerking.</span></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/centraal-bureau-voor-de-statistiek/wo-stage-onderzoek-milieukosten-mbv-bestaande-afval-en-emissiestatistieken-den-haag-201330","tags":["Afstudeerstage"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"wo-stage-woningmarkt-onderzoek-verhuisketens-doorstroom-en-ouderenwoningen-den-haag-321241","company_name":"Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek","title":"wo-stage woningmarkt onderzoek: verhuisketens, doorstroom en ouderenwoningen","description":"<h4 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">wo-</span><span style="color:#0580A1">afstudeerstage, </span><span style="color:#271D6C">vanaf februari 2027</span></span></strong></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Ben jij die analytische wo-student die nieuwsgierig is naar de doorstroom op de woningmarkt?<br>Krijg je energie van onderzoek doen, werken met data en programmeren in R?<br>Wil je jouw onderzoeksvaardigheden inzetten voor een actueel maatschappelijk vraagstuk?</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">uitdaging</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Verhuisketens geven inzicht in de doorstroom op de woningmarkt en zijn daardoor actueel en relevant. Het CBS heeft een methode ontwikkeld om deze ketens in beeld te brengen. Het dashboard </span><em><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://dashboards.cbs.nl/verhuisketens/"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Verhuisketens in Nederland</span></a></em><span style="font-size:1.2em"> toont onder meer de gemiddelde lengte van een verhuisketen. Er is echter nog veel ruimte voor verdieping.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Tijdens deze stage kun je afstudeeronderzoek doen naar de rol van ouderenwoningen in de doorstroom op de huizenmarkt. Je kunt daarin op zoek gaan naar antwoorden op de volgende vragen:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">In hoeverre draagt het bouwen van ouderenwoningen bij aan de doorstroom op de woningmarkt?</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Wat is de invloed van vergrijzing en overlijden van ouderen op de doorstroom en het woningaanbod?</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Heb je zelf een goede onderzoeksvraag die aansluit bij dit thema, dan is daar ook ruimte voor.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">stageplek </span><span style="color:#271D6C">bij CBS </span><span style="color:#0580A1">Den Haag</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#292A2E">De afdeling Beleidsstatistiek bestaat uit 70 collega’s verdeeld over Den Haag en Heerlen. Er werken onderzoekers en projectleiders met veel verschillende studieachtergronden binnen onze afdeling. Wij stellen cijfers samen die gebruikt worden voor het ontwikkelen, monitoren en verbeteren van beleid, vaak met een thema-overstijgend karakter. We zijn samenwerkingspartner op het gebied van data-gedreven werken bij overheden.</span></span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit breng </span><span style="color:#0580A1">jij</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> mee</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je bent bijna klaar met jouw wo master-opleiding in de sociale wetenschappen, demografie, ruimtelijke ordening of een aanverwante opleiding en zoekt een afstudeerstage om je opleiding succesvol af te ronden.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Daarnaast:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">heb je (enige) ervaring met programmeren in R;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">kun je zelfstandig onderzoek uitvoeren en uitkomsten analyseren;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">weet je hoe je met verschillende methoden en technieken onderzoek doet.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Kernwoorden die jou omschrijven zijn enthousiast, proactief en analytisch.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Omdat alle communicatie tijdens de stage – zowel mondeling als schriftelijk – in het Nederlands plaatsvindt, is een goede beheersing van de Nederlandse taal noodzakelijk.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit kun je van </span><span style="color:#0580A1">ons</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> verwachten</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een fijne leeromgeving waarin je:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw vakkennis vergroot en werkervaring opdoet;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">programmeervaardigheden toepast in de praktijk;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">leert werken met CBS-data.<br></span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Voor jouw inzet ontvang je een stagevergoeding van € 800 bruto per maand (op basis van 40 uur per week).</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Samen met je stagebegeleider stem je af hoe je hybride kunt werken, met flexibele werktijden en de optie om deels vanuit huis aan 