e:1.2em">Tijdens jouw stage bij het CBS duik je in de wereld van social media en ga je actief bijdragen aan het zichtbaar en begrijpelijk maken van belangrijke maatschappelijke cijfers.<br>Je krijgt de kans om jouw creativiteit in te zetten en verder te ontwikkelen. Je bedenkt nieuwe formats, werkt bestaande concepten uit en vertaalt complexe informatie naar content die mensen echt bereikt. Samen met het socialmediateam werk je aan sterke, herkenbare en aansprekende content.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Dit is wat je gaat doen:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je ontwikkelt creatieve socialmediaformats die aansluiten bij de doelgroep en strategie van het CBS.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je maakt content die daadwerkelijk wordt gepubliceerd op de socialmediakanalen van het CBS. Daarmee lever je een directe bijdrage aan de communicatie van een maatschappelijke organisatie.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je vertaalt statistische informatie naar heldere en toegankelijke verhalen voor een breed publiek.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je denkt actief mee over hoe het CBS zich creatief en onderscheidend kan positioneren op social media.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je draagt bij aan content die impact heeft: jouw werk wordt gezien door een groot publiek en helpt mensen Nederland en de cijfers beter te begrijpen.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit is jouw </span><span style="color:#0580A1">stageplek </span><span style="color:#271D6C">bij CBS </span><span style="color:#0580A1">Den Haag</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je komt terecht in het socialmediateam van het CBS: een klein, hecht team waarin we in een informele sfeer samenwerken. De lijnen zijn kort en er is volop ruimte om ideeën te delen en initiatief te nemen. <br>We zijn continu op zoek naar manieren om onze content beter, creatiever en relevanter te maken. Dat betekent dat we graag experimenteren met formats, inspelen op trends en openstaan voor frisse perspectieven.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit breng </span><span style="color:#0580A1">jij</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> mee</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je volgt een creatieve hbo-opleiding, zoals Communication &amp; Multimedia Design, Creative Business of een vergelijkbare opleiding.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je hebt kennis van en wellicht ervaring met:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Canva;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Adobe Creative Cloud;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">het monteren van short-formcontent;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">de nieuwste trends op social media.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je denkt in mogelijkheden en krijgt energie van samenwerken.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je hebt een ondernemende instelling en komt met innovatieve ideeën.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit kun je van </span><span style="color:#0580A1">ons</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> verwachten</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een fijne leeromgeving waarin je:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">jouw creatieve en socialmediaskills verder ontwikkelt in een professionele en informele werkomgeving;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">leert om complexe statistische informatie te vertalen naar begrijpelijke en toegankelijke content voor een breed publiek;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">effectief samenwerkt met betrokken collega's in een professioneel team.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Voor jouw inzet ontvang je een stagevergoeding van € 800,- bruto per maand (op basis van 40 uur per week).</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Samen met je stagebegeleider stem je af hoe je hybride kunt werken, met flexibele werktijden en de optie om deels vanuit huis aan jouw stageopdracht te werken.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit zijn </span><span style="color:#0580A1">onze</span><span style="color:#271D6C"> voorwaarden</span></span></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Het betreft een stageopdracht en geen werkervaringsplek. Voordat je aan de stage begint verwachten we dat je vanuit de onderwijsinstelling een stagebegeleider hebt, waarmee de stage is afgestemd en concrete leerdoelen zijn afgesproken. <br>Deze stageopdracht is bedoeld voor studenten die momenteel staan ingeschreven bij een onderwijsinstelling; afgestudeerden komen niet in aanmerking.</span></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/centraal-bureau-voor-de-statistiek/hbo-stage-social-media-content-creatie-den-haag-116363","tags":["Praktijkstage"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Den Haag, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"engineering-manager-mammography-amsterdam-rotterdam-272036","company_name":"DeepHealth","title":"Engineering Manager, Mammography","description":"<p style="text-align:start;">Job Summary</p><p style="text-align:start;">The Engineering Manager, Mammography leads the engineering team behind Mammo Dx, DeepHealth's FDA- and CE-cleared breast cancer detection AI for 2D mammography and 3D tomosynthesis, within the Clinical AI organization that brings together engineering, AI, clinical, and regulatory teams across the US and Europe. The role also acts as Technical Delivery Manager for the team, owning delivery of every release from plan to production. Working with the Mammo product lead, QRC, and US teams, the Engineering Manager, Mammography ensures the right software reaches the right sites on time, with the quality a medical device requires. The role reports to the Software Engineering Manager, Clinical AI Devices.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Essential Duties and Responsibilities</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Team Leadership &amp; Development</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Lead and mentor a team of 3 to 4 engineers; support their technical and professional growth.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Set clear goals, run regular 1:1s and performance reviews, and give constructive feedback.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Recruit, onboard and retain great engineers.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Foster a culture of ownership, quality and continuous improvement.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Release &amp; Delivery Management (TDM)</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Own the Mammo release plan jointly with the product lead: scope, sizing, milestones and monthly release tracking.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Drive each release end to end: planning, development, verification, regulatory sign-off, deployment and post-release follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Align the Mammo team's delivery practices, processes and tools with the Clinical AI standards.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Make sure test setups are ready so product can run functional validation on time.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Contribute to the 3- and 6-month roadmap rituals and keep delivery commitments predictable.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Quality &amp; Regulatory Compliance</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Work with QRC on regulatory impact assessments for every change.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;">Cross-Functional &amp; US Collaboration</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Communicate status, risks and trade-offs clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Coordinate with platform, AI and data teams on dependencies.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Technical Leadership</p><p style="text-align:start;">Take part in design and architecture reviews, challenge estimates and unblock the team.</p><p style="text-align:start;">Keep a strong grasp of the system without writing production code day to day.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">PLEASE NOTE: This is not an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities and requirements of the position described above. Other functions may be assigned and management retains the right to add or change duties at any time.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;">Minimum Qualifications, Education and Experience</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Bachelor's or master's degree in computer science, engineering or a related field, or equivalent experience (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">6+ years in software engineering, with a solid technical background (backend, cloud or data-heavy systems) (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">2+ years managing engineering teams (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Proven track record delivering software releases end to end: planning, QA, deployment and support (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Experience running delivery in a structured environment (regulated industry, enterprise B2B or on-premise deployments) (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Good understanding of modern engineering practices: CI/CD, cloud environments (AWS or GCP), containerized deployments (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">The right to work in France or the Netherlands (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Strong communication and leadership skills, with a focus on team collaboration and ownership (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Ability to mentor and organize a team of senior engineers (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Strong problem-solving and analytical skills (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Structured and reliable: people can count on plans and follow-up (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Comfortable working remotely, asynchronously, and across European and US time zones (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Fluent in English (required).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Preferred: Experience in medical device software (strong plus).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Preferred: Knowledge of DICOM and radiology workflows (PACS, RIS, modalities, HL7).</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"> Preferred: Experience with radiology AI, ideally mammography.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"> Preferred: Experience working with US-based teams and stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Quality Standards</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Communicates, cooperates, and consistently functions professionally and harmoniously with all levels of supervision, co-workers, visitors, and vendors.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Demonstrates initiative, personal awareness, professionalism and integrity, and exercises confidentiality in all areas of performance.· · Follows all local, regional and country laws concerning employment.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Follows all DeepHealth policies and procedures.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Follows data privacy, compliance, safety and confidentiality standards at all times.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Practices universal safety precautions.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Promotes good public relations on the phone and in person.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Adapts and is willing to learn new tasks, methods, and systems.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Reports to work regularly as scheduled; consistently punctual with respect to working hours, meal and rest breaks, and maintains satisfactory personal attendance in accordance with DeepHealth guidelines.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#7a7e8d">Completes job responsibilities in a quality and timely manner.</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Travel</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">This position requires domestic and international travel up to 10%, mainly to the US and within Europe.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Working Environment</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Remote, based in France or the Netherlands. Regular collaboration with US teams requires afternoon overlap with US time zones.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;">Physical Demands</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">The employee must be able to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Salary:</p><p>Paris: 60,000-80,000 EURO</p><p>Netherlands: 70,000-90,000 EURO</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/deephealth/engineering-manager-mammography-amsterdam-rotterdam-272036","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam / Rotterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793946683},{"slug":"strategy-operations-lead-data-intelligence-amsterdam-12335","company_name":"Gresb","title":"Strategy & Operations Lead, Data & Intelligence","description":"<p>GRESB is the global sustainability intelligence standard for real assets. For over 15 years, real estate and infrastructure managers have reported to us, building a dataset of 150,000+ assets across more than 2,000 portfolios. Together with Asset Impact, which tracks emissions for over 300,000 physical assets and 77,000 companies, we’re turning that data into decision-grade intelligence for investors, lenders, index providers and regulators.</p><p>We’re building a new Client &amp; Data Intelligence organization to showcase the value of the data to investors and develop new use cases within the ecosystem. It brings sales, product and data teams together under one leader, the Chief Client &amp; Data Intelligence Officer. This role is the person who makes that organization run. The role is based out of Amsterdam.</p><p><strong>The Role</strong></p><p>You’ll work directly with the Chief Client &amp; Data Intelligence Officer as the strategist and operator at the center of a newly formed team. Your job is to keep decisions moving, teams connected and priority work getting finished, so the leadership team can focus on clients and growth.</p><p>It’s a role for someone who can shape a problem and then see it through. One week you might be building the business case for a new data product; the next you’re tightening the sales pipeline, preparing a board update and unblocking a delivery issue between product and engineering. You’ll move between sales enablement, product and data operations, and you’ll be trusted to run several projects at once without dropping any of them.</p><p>You’ll see the whole business, from client conversations to product decisions to the CEO’s agenda, and you’ll have influence over how a new organization works.</p><p><strong>What you will do</strong></p><p><em>Strategy and priority projects</em></p><ul><li>Lead the organization’s highest-priority initiatives end to end, for example pricing, our investor program, entry into new markets and maturing the data strategy</li><li>Frame the problem, build the analysis, align stakeholders and drive the work through to a decision and implementation</li><li>Bring a recommendation, not just options</li></ul><p><em>Operating rhythm and decision-making</em></p><ul><li>Run the team’s operating cadence: weekly deal desk, fortnightly product council and monthly business review</li><li>Own the decision log, so it’s always clear what was decided, by whom and what happens next</li><li>Spot blockers between sales, product and data teams early and clear them</li></ul><p><em>Commercial operations and sales enablement</em></p><ul><li>Own pricing and support deal structuring with the sales team</li><li>Keep pipeline and ARR reporting accurate and trusted, with one view across GRESB</li><li>Work with sales and product to make sure the team has what it needs to showcase the value of the data products</li></ul><p><em>Reporting and communication</em></p><ul><li>Build and run the monthly CEO dashboard and KPI reporting</li><li>Prepare senior leadership, board and client materials that are clear, concise and decision-ready</li><li>Act as the Chief Client &amp; Data Intelligence Officer’s point of contact when they’re away</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>What success looks like</strong></p><p>In your first six months</p><ul><li>The operating rhythm is running and people rely on it</li><li>The decision log is live and used</li><li>There’s one trusted ARR view across GRESB data products</li></ul><p>By the end of your first year</p><ul><li>At least two priority projects have been taken from problem to implemented decision</li><li>Leadership and board reporting runs on a predictable monthly cycle with little rework</li><li>Sales, product and data teams describe fewer handoff issues, and escalations get resolved faster</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Around 6–10 years of experience</li><li>A grounding in top-tier management consulting or Big Four advisory, in strategy, sustainability, data or technology</li><li>Ideally, spent time at a sustainability data, ESG ratings, real asset or financial data business</li><li>Strong business acumen and ability to work well in a cross-functional, global environment.</li><li>Experience implementing AI or advanced analytics solutions within a commercial or sales environment.</li><li>Proficiency in CRM, data analytics, and visualization tools.</li><li>A working understanding of how data products are packaged, priced and sold</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>How you work</strong></p><ul><li>You think in structure: you can break down an ambiguous problem, find what matters and build a clear path forward</li><li>You finish things. You run several projects at once and see each one through to the end</li><li>You’re organized, detail-oriented and work well in systems</li><li>You write and present clearly, whether it’s a one-page update or a board deck</li><li>You get things done without formal authority, by earning trust across sales, product and engineering</li><li>You’re comfortable moving between the big picture and the detail in the same day</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Involvement in a fast growing international data-driven company</li><li>Opportunity to work with a highly talented and committed team in a supportive environment with strong camaraderie</li><li>Annual leave of 25 days per calendar year</li><li>2 volunteering days off per year</li><li>Company pension plan</li><li>Free public transport to and from the Amsterdam office</li><li>Free and healthy office lunch catered daily&nbsp;</li><li>Annual professional development budget</li><li>Home office budget&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>About GRESB</strong></p><p>GRESB is the global sustainability intelligence standard for real assets. We transform sustainability data into decision-grade intelligence that drives capital allocation and asset improvement.</p><p><strong>Our vision:&nbsp;</strong>An investment industry that plays a central role in creating a sustainable world.</p><p><strong>Our mission:</strong>&nbsp;To provide financial markets with actionable sustainability insights, data, and benchmarks. More than 100 global institutional and financial investors rely on GRESB to help guide their investment decisions, mitigating risk, improving portfolio quality, and driving long-term financial success.</p><p>The GRESB team is an energetic group of more than 100 individuals from diverse backgrounds with experience spanning sustainability, data science, software development, real estate, infrastructure, and the capital markets. Most of us work out of our head office in Amsterdam or one of our satellite offices in London, Paris, Berlin, Boston, Singapore, or Sydney. We’re passionate about tackling the sustainability challenge by providing the insights that will power the markets of the future and enable investors to allocate the world’s capital in a more responsible way.</p><p>GRESB is a portfolio company of BeyondNetZero, General Atlantic's climate investing platform.</p><p>GRESB is an equitable, diverse, and inclusive workplace, one at which all workers - regardless of their gender, race, ethnicity, national origin, age, sexual orientation, identity, education, or disability - feel valued and respected. We are committed to a non-discriminatory approach to hiring and provide equal opportunity for employment and advancement in all of our teams and programs.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/gresb/strategy-operations-lead-data-intelligence-amsterdam-12335","tags":["Commercial Real Estate","Business development"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","created_at":1793938810},{"slug":"senior-fleet-manager-barneveld-465518","company_name":"Orion","title":"Senior Fleet Manager","description":"<p><span style="color:#121317">Ben jij een vooruitdenker die complexe data moeiteloos vertaalt naar glashelder advies? Neem jij van nature de regie, ben je sterk in stakeholdermanagement en heb je affiniteit met de dynamische wereld van Schiphol? Lees dan snel verder!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Binnen Orion Fleet Management zijn we op zoek naar een proactieve Senior Fleet Manager met een specifieke focus op onze klant Schiphol en ons label AirportPartners.&nbsp;Waar een reguliere Fleet Manager sterk leunt op de dagelijkse operatie, sta jij als Senior Fleet Manager daarboven. Jij kijkt verder dan de waan van de dag, anticipeert op wat komen gaat en gebruikt keiharde data om onze klant op strategisch niveau te adviseren.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Wat ga je doen?</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#121317">In de rol van Senior Fleet Manager ben jij de absolute eigenaar van de vlootbeschikbaarheid voor Schiphol. Met ons label AirportPartners beheren wij hier de unieke en bedrijfskritische vloot van Schiphol: van de brandweerwagens en de onmisbare sneeuwvloot tot de personenwagens van het KLM-personeel.&nbsp;Jouw werk draait niet om achteraf reageren, maar om proactief sturen. Omdat jij de operationele basis feilloos begrijpt en beheerst, kun jij de vertaalslag maken naar optimalisatie en strategisch partnership.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Jouw takenpakket als Senior Fleet Manager bestaat uit de volgende pijlers:</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u><span style="color:#000000">Datagedreven Regie &amp; Strategie:</span></u></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Proactieve advisering:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je wacht niet tot de klant belt met een probleem, maar je adviseert hen ongevraagd over rendementsverbetering en risicobeperking op basis van jouw data-analyses;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Datagedreven regie:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je gebruikt voorspellende data om de vloot optimaal in te zetten en stilstand te minimaliseren. Vooruitdenken is jouw tweede natuur;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Bewaking van SLA’s en KPI’s:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je monitort continu de prestaties, stuurt bij waar nodig en garandeert dat we onze beloftes aan de klant waarmaken (of overtreffen);</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Rapportage en overleg:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je zit regelmatig aan tafel met het management van klanten en leveranciers. Je presenteert heldere rapportages en treedt op als een volwaardig en strategisch gesprekspartner.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong><u><span style="color:#000000">Operationele Excellentie:</span></u></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Om op strategisch niveau te kunnen adviseren, zorg jij dat de basisprocessen, de motor van de afdeling, vlekkeloos verlopen:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Triage en analyse:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je overziet de storingsmeldingen en zorgt voor een feilloze initiële beoordeling.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Slimme planning:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> </span><span style="color:#121317">Je overziet de planning van (preventief) onderhoud, altijd met de impact op de 24/7 luchthaven operatie en veiligheid op Schiphol in je achterhoofd;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Toetsing en beoordeling:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je beoordeelt complexe reparatie aanvragen kritisch op basis van historie, vastgelegde afspraken en toekomstige inzet van het voertuig;</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Wat vragen we van jou?</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#121317">Voor de rol van Senior Fleet Manager zoeken we iemand die stevig in zijn of haar schoenen staat. Je overziet het grote geheel, maar snapt de details die de data beïnvloeden. Verder zien wij graag het volgende terug:</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Denkniveau:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je beschikt over HBO of WO werk- en denkniveau;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Sterk analytisch:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je bent een kei in het analyseren van data en haalt hier moeiteloos de juiste conclusies en actiepunten uit;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Proactieve mindset:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je wacht niet af, maar signaleert kansen en knelpunten voordat ze een probleem vormen;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Kennis &amp; Ervaring:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je snapt hoe onderhoudsprocessen (triage, MTTR, MTBF) werken. Ervaring als Fleet Manager is een must en ervaring in de automotive of specifiek de OV-sector (bussen) is een zware pré;</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Overtuigingskracht:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Je hebt uitstekende communicatieve vaardigheden. Je kunt draagvlak creëren en complexe technische of data-gerelateerde zaken begrijpelijk uitleggen aan directie, klanten en leveranciers.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Ben jij klaar voor deze stap als Senior Fleet Manager en wil je bouwen aan de toekomst van ons wagenparkbeheer op Schiphol? Druk dan snel op de sollicitatieknop en laat jouw cv en motivatie achter!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Wat bieden wij</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#121317">Een leuke en uitdagende baan met veel zelfstandigheid en verantwoordelijkheid. Je komt te werken in een professionele en stabiele kantooromgeving. Orion is een sterk groeiend bedrijf binnen de Pon-onderneming en biedt doorgroeimogelijkheden in de toekomst.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Wat bieden we nog meer voor de functie van Senior Fleet Manager:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een goed salaris tussen de € 4.579,- en € 6.538,- o.b.v. fulltime. Uiteraard is dit afhankelijk van jouw kennis en ervaring;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">28 vakantiedagen* en 6 ADV dagen;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een individueel keuzebudget (o.a. te besteden voor het aankopen van verlof);</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Directe en korte lijnen; je rapporteert rechtstreeks aan de Teamlead Operations;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">De mogelijkheid om deels thuis te werken;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een enthousiast, gezellig, compact en ambitieus team;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een ruime Pon-pensioenregeling;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een collectieve ziektekostenverzekering bij ONVZ of Zilveren Kruis waarbij Pon €300 per jaar bijdraagt;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Pon Fit: sportieve activiteiten waar je aan kan deelnemen! Van bootcamp tot golfclinic;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Korting op eigen producten van Pon (bijv. een nieuwe Gazelle fiets of privé lease auto), €500 per jaar;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Lease-a-bike regeling voor het leasen van een Pon-fiets.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Over de organisatie</span></strong></h3><p><span style="color:#000000">Orion ontzorgt bedrijven met grote complexe wagenparken door het reparatie- en onderhoudsproces optimaal te structureren. <br><br>Binnen het netwerk heeft Orion een 15-tal eigen werkplaatsen onder de labels: AirportPartners, BusPartners en WastePartners. Onze werkplaatsen zijn gevestigd in: Almere, Amersfoort, Badhoevedorp-Schiphol (2 locaties), Ede, Emmeloord, Helmond, Leeuwarden, Leiden, Lichtenvoorde, Middelburg, Montfoort, Oosterwolde, Utrecht en Zwolle. Deze vacature is gericht op ons hoofdkantoor in Barneveld!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Met circa 250 collega’s zetten wij ons dagelijks in om ervoor te zorgen dat onder andere huis en bedrijfsafval opgehaald kunnen worden, vliegtuigen kunnen blijven opstijgen en landen en OV-reizigers in veilige en betrouwbare bussen kunnen reizen.&nbsp;Wij staan midden in de maatschappij en spelen in op trends als verstedelijking, elektrificatie, duurzaamheid en digitalisering.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Iedereen is welkom !</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Bij Orion en Pon maken de mensen het verschil. Wij geloven dat een diverse en inclusieve organisatie zorgt voor meer werkplezier, creativiteit en betere resultaten. Welke achtergrond, leeftijd of identiteit je ook meebrengt: als jij de motivatie en het talent hebt, horen we heel graag van je.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br><span style="color:#121317">Heb je vragen over de vacature of de sollicitatieprocedure? Neem gerust contact op met Wesley Bruinier (Recruiter) via +316 26 13 82 54 of </span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="color:#121317">.</span></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/orion/senior-fleet-manager-barneveld-465518","tags":["Overig"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Barneveld, Gelderland, Nederland","created_at":1793935913},{"slug":"go-to-market-associate-amsterdam-480909","company_name":"LLEVERAGE","title":"Go-To-Market Associate","description":"<h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">About us</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">Hey there! We're Lleverage, and we're making the </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Autonomous Back Office</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> actually achievable for businesses. We enable teams to capture, automate, and integrate AI agents into their business, because AI is only useful when it actually fits into daily operations.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#222222">We help the most strategic European industries – manufacturing, logistics, and wholesale – automate the messy, manual processes that most tools can’t handle. </span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#222222">We’re a fast-growing, VC-backed scale-up based in Amsterdam, with big ambitions for 2026 and beyond. This is your chance to join early, have real impact, and grow alongside the company. </span><span style="color:#000000">If that sounds something you want to help build, we'd love to have you on board!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">About the role</span></strong></h4><p><span style="color:#000000">We're looking for an exceptional Go-To-Market Associate who will be the engine of our commercial team. As part of the top 1% of Commercial talents globally, you'll combine systematic prospecting with creative outreach to build relationships with decision-makers who need AI solutions. </span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">This is not a classic sales role. We're looking for a builder with a commercial brain and an enormous drive, someone who combines hustle, strategic creativity, and genuine curiosity about what makes businesses tick.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">You might come from a classic sales background, or you might have built your commercial instincts in a completely different arena. What matters far more than your CV is your drive, your entrepreneurial instinct, and the kind of work ethic that makes people wonder how you get so much done.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">In a single day you might: map a new industry vertical for outreach opportunities, run a consultative discovery call with a Head of Operations at a manufacturing company, develop a proposal for a new channel, follow up on an active deal in scoping, and draft a business case for entering a completely new market.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]" style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">You won't have a large team behind you. You will have full autonomy, meaningful equity, direct access to the founding team, and the freedom to experiment with what works.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Why Lleverage?</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Change the world, literally</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: 2026 is the year AI works, and </span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://Lleverage.ai">Lleverage.ai</a><span style="color:#000000"> has the best AI platform (according to industry veterans)</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Work, learn, have fun</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: You'll be part of a top-notch commercial team that operates at the highest level of performance</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Build a unique network</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: Connect with decision-makers and operational leaders across traditional industries who are eager to implement AI solutions</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Get autonomy &amp; ownership</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: Design your own strategies and own your pipeline development</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Compensation</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">: We pay top of market cash and equity, with compensation tied to the pipeline value you create</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Responsibilities</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Own our top of funnel:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> which segments we go after, how we reach the COOs and CFOs of manufacturers and distributors, and how many qualified opportunities land in the pipeline every week. That's your number.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Sit in on live deals from day one</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">: discovery calls, account plans, proposals and PoC scoping with our delivery team. Within 6 to 12 months you run your first deals yourself.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Build the playbook with the GTM lead and CCO:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> positioning per sector, messaging per persona, pricing experiments, the business cases we win with.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Run experiments across the whole funnel:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> outbound campaigns, events, partnerships with ERP partners and PE firms, LinkedIn content. Measure everything, scale what works.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Use AI-native tooling</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> (Clay, lemlist, our own agents) to research, personalise and scale what a team of five used to do by hand, and help us figure out what GTM looks like when AI does the grunt work.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Bring what you see in the market to the founding team and product:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> which use cases, sectors, competitors and prices we should bet on next.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong><span style="color:#000000">Job specific requirements</span></strong></h4><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">1 to 3 years in consulting, investment banking, PE or a fast-growing B2B startup, or you built something yourself.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You make things happen without a brief, and can show it with an example and a number.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You win trust fast, with a CFO in a boardroom and with an operations manager on a factory floor.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You think in funnels and business cases and turn data into a clear recommendation.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">New sectors, no playbook, channels nobody has tried: that energises you rather than stops you. A no on Monday doesn't define your Tuesday.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Genuinely curious about how businesses make money and where they lose it.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You want to own revenue within a year and know why.</span></p>